

relation Type_alpha: `typeIR''''` and `typeIR'''''`


. If let `baseTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `baseTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `baseTypeIR` is equal to `baseTypeIR'`.
 .. Group basetype:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TID tid` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `TID tid'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group nametype:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `polyTypeDefIR~a~ < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `polyTypeDefIR~b~ < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group spectype:
  ... Let `typeIR~a_spec~` be `<<specialize_typeDef, $specialize_typeDef(polyTypeDefIR~a~, typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~b_spec~` be `<<specialize_typeDef, $specialize_typeDef(polyTypeDefIR~b~, typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a_spec~` and `typeIR~b_spec~` are the same type>>:
   .... If `<<is_nominal_typeIR, $is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~a_spec~)>> /\ <<is_nominal_typeIR, $is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~b_spec~)>>`:
    ..... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... The relation holds.
   .... Else if `~<<is_nominal_typeIR, $is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~a_spec~)>> /\ ~<<is_nominal_typeIR, $is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~b_spec~)>>`:
    ..... The relation holds.
. Group typedeftype:
 .. If let `TYPEDEF _ typeIR~a~` be `typeIR''''`:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR'''''` are the same type>>:
   .... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `TYPEDEF _ typeIR~b~` be `typeIR'''''`:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR''''` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. If let `TYPE tid typeIR~a~` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `TYPE tid' typeIR~b~` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group newtype:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `LIST < typeIR~a~ >` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `LIST < typeIR~b~ >` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group listtype:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TUPLE < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `TUPLE < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group tupletype:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `typeIR~a~ [ n~s~ ]` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `typeIR~b~ [ n~s'~ ]` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `n~s~` is equal to `n~s'~`.
 .. Group stacktype:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `STRUCT tid { typeIR~f_a~ id~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `STRUCT tid' { typeIR~f_b~ id~f'~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `id~f~` is equal to `id~f'~`, for all `id~f~` in `id~f~^{asterisk}^` and `id~f'~` in `id~f'~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group structtype:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~f_a~` and `typeIR~f_b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~f_a~` in `typeIR~f_a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~f_b~` in `typeIR~f_b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `HEADER tid { typeIR~f_a~ id~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `HEADER tid' { typeIR~f_b~ id~f'~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `id~f~` is equal to `id~f'~`, for all `id~f~` in `id~f~^{asterisk}^` and `id~f'~` in `id~f'~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group headertype:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~f_a~` and `typeIR~f_b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~f_a~` in `typeIR~f_a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~f_b~` in `typeIR~f_b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `HEADER_UNION tid { typeIR~f_a~ id~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `HEADER_UNION tid' { typeIR~f_b~ id~f'~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `id~f~` is equal to `id~f'~`, for all `id~f~` in `id~f~^{asterisk}^` and `id~f'~` in `id~f'~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group headeruniontype:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~f_a~` and `typeIR~f_b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~f_a~` in `typeIR~f_a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~f_b~` in `typeIR~f_b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. If let `ENUM tid { id~f~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `enumTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
  ... Let!~type~ `ENUM tid' { id~f'~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `id~f~` is equal to `id~f'~`, for all `id~f~` in `id~f~^{asterisk}^` and `id~f'~` in `id~f'~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
  ... Group enumtype:
   .... The relation holds.
 .. Else let `ENUM tid # typeIR~a~ { id~f~ = value~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `enumTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
  ... Let!~type~ `ENUM tid' # typeIR~b~ { id~f'~ = value~f'~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `id~f~` is equal to `id~f'~`, for all `id~f~` in `id~f~^{asterisk}^` and `id~f'~` in `id~f'~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
  ... Check that `value~f~` is equal to `value~f'~`, for all `value~f~` in `value~f~^{asterisk}^` and `value~f'~` in `value~f'~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Group serenumtype:
   .... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>:
    ..... The relation holds.
. Else if let `EXTERN tid { rid~a~ : routineTypeDefIR~a~^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `EXTERN tid' { rid~b~ : routineTypeDefIR~b~^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group externtype:
  ... Check that <<eq_set, `{ rid~a~^{asterisk}^ }` is equal to `{ rid~b~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `routineTypeDefIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `routineTypeDefIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>({ rid~a~ : routineTypeDefIR~a~^{asterisk}^ }, rid~a~)>>`.
--
+
for each `rid~a~` in `rid~a~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Check that `routineTypeDefIR^?^` is Some value, for all `routineTypeDefIR^?^` in `routineTypeDefIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR~a'~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `routineTypeDefIR~a'~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `?routineTypeDefIR~a'~` be `routineTypeDefIR^?^`.
--
+
for each `routineTypeDefIR^?^` in `routineTypeDefIR^?^^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR'^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `routineTypeDefIR'^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `routineTypeDefIR'^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>({ rid~b~ : routineTypeDefIR~b~^{asterisk}^ }, rid~a~)>>`.
--
+
for each `rid~a~` in `rid~a~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Check that `routineTypeDefIR'^?^` is Some value, for all `routineTypeDefIR'^?^` in `routineTypeDefIR'^?^^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR~b'~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `routineTypeDefIR~b'~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `?routineTypeDefIR~b'~` be `routineTypeDefIR'^?^`.
--
+
for each `routineTypeDefIR'^?^` in `routineTypeDefIR'^?^^{asterisk}^`
  ... If <<RoutineTypeDef_alpha, `routineTypeDefIR~a'~` and `routineTypeDefIR~b'~` are the same type>>, for all `routineTypeDefIR~a'~` in `routineTypeDefIR~a'~^{asterisk}^` and `routineTypeDefIR~b'~` in `routineTypeDefIR~b'~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `PARSER ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `PARSER ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group parsertype:
  ... If <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `CONTROL ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `CONTROL ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group controltype:
  ... If <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `PACKAGE < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `PACKAGE < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group packagetype:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TABLE tid # typeIR~a~` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `TABLE tid' # typeIR~b~` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group tabletype:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `defaultTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `defaultTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group defaulttype:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `sequenceTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. If let `SEQ < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `sequenceTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `sequenceTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
  ... Let!~type~ `SEQ < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `sequenceTypeIR'`.
  ... Group sequencetype:
   .... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... The relation holds.
 .. Else let `SEQ < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ , ... >` be `sequenceTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `sequenceTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
  ... Let!~type~ `SEQ < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ , ... >` be `sequenceTypeIR'`.
  ... Group sequencedefaulttype:
   .... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... The relation holds.
. Else if let `recordTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. If let `RECORD { typeIR~a~ id ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `recordTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `recordTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
  ... Let!~type~ `RECORD { typeIR~b~ id' ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `recordTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `id` is equal to `id'`, for all `id` in `id^{asterisk}^` and `id'` in `id'^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Group recordtype:
   .... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... The relation holds.
 .. Else let `RECORD { typeIR~a~ id ;^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `recordTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `recordTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
  ... Let!~type~ `RECORD { typeIR~b~ id' ;^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `recordTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `id` is equal to `id'`, for all `id` in `id^{asterisk}^` and `id'` in `id'^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Group recorddefaulttype:
   .... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... The relation holds.
. Else if let `invalidHeaderTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `invalidHeaderTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group invalidtype:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `SET < typeIR^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Let!~type~ `[typeIR~a~]` be `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let!~type~ `SET < typeIR''^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Let!~type~ `[typeIR~b~]` be `typeIR''^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group settype:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `tableMetadataTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. If let `TABLE_ENUM tid { id~f~^{asterisk}^ }` be `tableMetadataTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `tableMetadataTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
  ... Let!~type~ `TABLE_ENUM tid' { id~f'~^{asterisk}^ }` be `tableMetadataTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `id~f~` is equal to `id~f'~`, for all `id~f~` in `id~f~^{asterisk}^` and `id~f'~` in `id~f'~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
  ... Group tableenumtype:
   .... The relation holds.
 .. Else let `TABLE_STRUCT tid { typeIR~f_a~ id~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `tableMetadataTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `tableMetadataTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
  ... Let!~type~ `TABLE_STRUCT tid' { typeIR~f_b~ id~f'~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `tableMetadataTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `id~f~` is equal to `id~f'~`, for all `id~f~` in `id~f~^{asterisk}^` and `id~f'~` in `id~f'~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
  ... Group tablestructtype:
   .... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~f_a~` and `typeIR~f_b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~f_a~` in `typeIR~f_a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~f_b~` in `typeIR~f_b~^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... The relation holds.


relation ParameterType_alpha: `_ typeIR~a~ _ _^?^` and `_ typeIR~b~ _ _^?^`


. Group :
 .. If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>:
  ... The relation holds.


relation RoutineType_alpha: `routineTypeIR` and `routineTypeIR'`


. If let `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR'`.
 .. Group action:
  ... If <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `routineTypeIR'`.
 .. Group function:
  ... If <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>:
    ..... The relation holds.
. Else if let `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `routineTypeIR'`.
 .. Group externfunction:
  ... If <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>:
    ..... The relation holds.
. Else if let `BUILTIN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `BUILTIN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `routineTypeIR'`.
 .. Group builtinmethod:
  ... If <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>:
    ..... The relation holds.
. Else if let `externMethodTypeIR` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. If let `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `externMethodTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `externMethodTypeIR'` be `routineTypeIR'`.
  ... Let!~type~ `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `externMethodTypeIR'`.
  ... Group externmethod:
   .... If <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>:
     ...... The relation holds.
 .. Else let `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `externMethodTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `externMethodTypeIR'` be `routineTypeIR'`.
  ... Let!~type~ `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `externMethodTypeIR'`.
  ... Group externmethod-abstract:
   .... If <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>:
     ...... The relation holds.
. Else if let `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR'`.
 .. Group parserapply:
  ... If <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR'`.
 .. Group controlapply:
  ... If <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else let `TABLE_APPLY -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `TABLE_APPLY -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `routineTypeIR'`.
 .. Group tableapply:
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>:
   .... The relation holds.


relation RoutineTypeDef_alpha: `routineTypeDefIR` and `routineTypeDefIR'`


. If let `routineTypeIR~a~` be `routineTypeDefIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `routineTypeIR~b~` be `routineTypeDefIR'`.
 .. Group mono:
  ... If <<RoutineType_alpha, `routineTypeIR~a~` and `routineTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else let `routineTypeIR~a~ < tid~a~^{asterisk}^ , tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `routineTypeDefIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `routineTypeIR~b~ < tid~b~^{asterisk}^ , tid~hidden_b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `routineTypeDefIR'`.
 .. Group poly:
  ... Check that the length of `tid~a~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `tid~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that the length of `tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `tid~hidden_b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be <<fresh_tids, `the length of tid~a~^{asterisk}^ + the length of tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^` fresh type variables>>.
  ... Let `tid~a'~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~a~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `theta~a~` be `{ tid~a'~ : TID tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `routineTypeIR~a_subst~` be `<<subst_routineType, $subst_routineType(theta~a~, routineTypeIR~a~)>>`.
  ... Let `tid~b'~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~b~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~hidden_b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `theta~b~` be `{ tid~b'~ : TID tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `routineTypeIR~b_subst~` be `<<subst_routineType, $subst_routineType(theta~b~, routineTypeIR~b~)>>`.
  ... If <<RoutineType_alpha, `routineTypeIR~a_subst~` and `routineTypeIR~b_subst~` are the same type>>:
   .... The relation holds.


relation Type_wf: `bound` and `typeIR'''`


. If let `baseTypeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group baseTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TID tid` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group nameTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<in_set, `tid` is an element of the set `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `polyTypeDefIR < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group specializedTypeIR:
  ... Let `typeIR` be `<<specialize_typeDef, $specialize_typeDef(polyTypeDefIR, typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... If <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TYPEDEF _ typeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group typedefTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<nestable_typedef, `typeIR` can be used in a typedef>>.
  ... If <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TYPE _ typeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group newTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<nestable_new, `typeIR` can be used in a new type>>.
  ... If <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `LIST < typeIR >` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group listTypeIR:
