relation Eval_static: `p`, `TC`, and `expressionIR # ( _ _ )`


. If let `booleanLiteral` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-boolean:
  ... If `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `TRUE`:
   .... Result in `B true`.
  ... Else `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `FALSE`:
   .... Result in `B false`.
. Else if let `numberLiteral` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-number:
  ... If let `D i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Result in `D i`.
  ... Else if let `n W i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Result in `n W i`.
  ... Else let `n S i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Result in `n S i`.
. Else if let `" text "` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-stringLiteral:
  ... Result in `" text "`.
. Else if let `prefixedNameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value` be `<<find_value, $find_value(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `value`.
. Else if let `defaultExpression` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group defaultExpressionIR:
  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.
. Else if let `unop typedExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group unaryExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in <<un_op, `unop` `value`>>.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~l~ binop' typedExpressionIR~r~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group binaryExpressionIR:
  ... Check that `~binop' is in [&&, ||]`.
  ... Let `value~l~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in <<bin_op, `value~l~` `binop'` `value~r~`>>.
  ... If `binop'` matches pattern `&&`:
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Result in `B false`.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Result in `value~r~`.
  ... Else if `binop'` matches pattern `||`:
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Result in `B true`.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Result in `value~r~`.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~cond~ ? typedExpressionIR~true~ : typedExpressionIR~false~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group ternaryExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~cond~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
   .... Let `value~true~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~true~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Result in `value~true~`.
  ... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
   .... Let `value~false~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~false~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Result in `value~false~`.
. Else if let `( typeIR ) typedExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group castExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `value~cast~` be `<<cast_op, $cast_op(typeIR, value)>>`.
  ... Result in `value~cast~`.
. Else if let `dataExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Check that `dataExpressionIR` matches pattern `{#}`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-invalid:
  ... Result in `{#}`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-sequence:
  ... If let `SEQ { typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let `value^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR` in `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`
   .... Result in `SEQ ( value^{asterisk}^ )`.
  ... Else if let `SEQ { typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let `value^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR` in `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`
   .... Result in `SEQ ( value^{asterisk}^ , ... )`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-record:
  ... If let `RECORD { nameIR = typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let `value^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR` in `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`
   .... Result in `RECORD { value nameIR ;^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Else if let `RECORD { nameIR = typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let `value^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR` in `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`
   .... Result in `RECORD { value nameIR ;^{asterisk}^ , ... }`.
. Else if let `ERROR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group errorAccessExpressionIR:
  ... Let `nameIR~error~` be `"error." ++ nameIR`.
  ... Let `value~error~` be `<<find_value, $find_value(p, TC, ` nameIR~error~)>>`.
  ... Result in `value~error~`.
. Else if let `memberAccessBaseIR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Else if let `TYPE prefixedNameIR` be `memberAccessBaseIR`:
  ... Group memberAccessExpressionIR-type:
   .... Let!~option~ `typeDefIR` be `<<find_type, $find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `enumTypeIR` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... If let `ENUM tid { id~member~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `id~member~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Result in `tid . nameIR`.
   .... Else let `ENUM tid # typeIR { id~member~ = value~member~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Let!~option~ `value` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<id, value>(nameIR, (id~member~, value~member~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
    ..... Result in `tid . nameIR # value`.
 .. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be `memberAccessBaseIR`:
  ... Check that `nameIR` is equal to `"size"`.
  ... Group memberAccessExpressionIR-expression-stack-size:
   .... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ _ )` be `typedExpressionIR~base~`.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let!~type~ `_ [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR`.
   .... Result in `D n~size~`.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ]` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group sliceAccessExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value~base~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `value~hi~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~hi~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `value~lo~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~lo~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in `<<bitacc_op, $bitacc_op(value~base~, value~hi~, value~lo~)>>`.
. Else if let `callExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callExpressionIR`.
 .. Else if `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
  ... Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Group callExpressionIR-builtin-size:
   .... If let `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR` be `routineTargetIR`:
    ..... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ _ )` be `typedExpressionIR~base~`.
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
    ..... Result in `<<sizeof, $sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)>>`.
   .... Else if let `TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR` be `routineTargetIR`:
    ..... Let!~option~ `typeDefIR` be `<<find_type, $find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
    ..... If let `typeIR~base~` be `typeDefIR`:
     ...... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
     ...... Result in `<<sizeof, $sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)>>`.
    ..... Else let `typeIR~base~ < tid^{asterisk}^ , tid'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeDefIR`:
     ...... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
     ...... Check that `tid'^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
     ...... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
     ...... Result in `<<sizeof, $sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)>>`.
 .. Else if let `( routineTargetIR )` be `routineTargetIR`:
  ... Group callExpressionIR-parenthesized:
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) # ( _ _ )`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Result in `value`.
. Else if let `( typedExpressionIR )` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group parenthesizedExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in `value`.


relation Type_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `typeOrVoid`


. Group primitiveType:
 .. If `typeOrVoid` matches pattern `VOID`:
  ... Result in the type `VOID` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Else if `typeOrVoid` is equal to `BOOL`:
  ... Result in the type `BOOL` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Else if `typeOrVoid` is equal to `ERROR`:
  ... Result in the type `ERROR` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Else if `typeOrVoid` is equal to `MATCH_KIND`:
  ... Result in the type `MATCH_KIND` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Else if `typeOrVoid` is equal to `STRING`:
  ... Result in the type `STRING` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. If let `baseType` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Check that `baseType` matches pattern `INT`.
 .. Group arbint:
  ... Result in the type `INT` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Group fixint:
  ... If let `INT < int >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let!~type~ `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `INT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else if let `INT < ( expression ) >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `INT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Group fixbit:
  ... If `baseType` matches pattern `BIT`:
   .... Result in the type `BIT < 1 >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else if let `BIT < int >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let!~type~ `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `BIT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else if let `BIT < ( expression ) >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `BIT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Group varbit:
  ... If let `VARBIT < int >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let!~type~ `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `VARBIT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else if let `VARBIT < ( expression ) >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `VARBIT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Else if let `prefixedTypeName` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Group prefixedTypeName:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typeDefIR` be `<<find_type, $find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... If let `typeIR` be `typeDefIR`:
   .... Result in the type `typeIR` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else let `polyTypeDefIR` be `typeDefIR`:
   .... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR < [ ] >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Else if let `prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList' >` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Group specializedType:
  ... If `typeArgumentList'` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `typeDefIR` be `<<find_type, $find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `typeIR` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... Result in the type `typeIR` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
  ... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `<<find_type, $find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Else if let `?typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`:
   .... Let!~type~ `polyTypeDefIR` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... Let `typeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >` be `polyTypeDefIR`.
   .... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeArgumentList, the list of type arguments in `typeArgumentList'`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `namedType [ expression~size~ ]` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Group headerStackType:
  ... If let `prefixedTypeName` be `namedType`:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `prefixedTypeName`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~size~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `value~size~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~size~)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `n~size~` be `int`.
   .... Let `typeIR~stack~` be `TID "T" [ n~size~ ]`.
   .... Let `polyTypeDefIR~stack~` be `typeIR~stack~ < ["T"] , [ ] >`.
   .... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR~stack~ < [typeIR~base~] >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else let `specializedType` be `namedType`:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `specializedType`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~size~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `value~size~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~size~)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `n~size~` be `int`.
   .... Let `typeIR~stack~` be `TID "T" [ n~size~ ]`.
   .... Let `polyTypeDefIR~stack~` be `typeIR~stack~ < ["T"] , [ ] >`.
   .... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR~stack~ < [typeIR~base~] >` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `LIST < typeArgument >` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Group listType:
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArgument_ok, typing `typeArgument`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~list~` be `LIST < TID "T" >`.
  ... Let `polyTypeDefIR~list~` be `typeIR~list~ < ["T"] , [ ] >`.
  ... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR~list~ < [typeIR~arg~] >` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `TUPLE < typeArgumentList >` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Group tupleType:
  ... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeArgumentList, the list of type arguments in `typeArgumentList`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `i~idx~^{asterisk}^` be `<<init_, $init_(the length of typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~tparam~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~tparam~` be `"T" ++ <<int_to_text, $int_to_text(i~idx~)>>`.
--
+
for each `i~idx~` in `i~idx~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeIR~tuple~` be `TUPLE < TID tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^ >`.
  ... Let `polyTypeDefIR~tuple~` be `typeIR~tuple~ < tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^ , [ ] >`.
  ... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR~tuple~ < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.


relation TypeArgument_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `typeArgument`


. If let `type` be `typeArgument`:
 .. Group type:
  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the type argument `typeIR` and set of fresh type variables `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `nonTypeName` be `typeArgument`:
 .. Group nonTypeName:
  ... Let `tid` be <<name, the name of `nonTypeName`>>.
  ... Result in the type argument `TID tid` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Let!~type~ `realTypeArgument` be `typeArgument`.
. If `realTypeArgument` matches pattern `VOID`:
 .. Group void:
  ... Result in the type argument `VOID` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Else if `realTypeArgument` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare:
  ... Let `tid~impl~` be <<fresh_tid, a fresh type variable>>.
  ... Result in the type argument `TID tid~impl~` and set of fresh type variables `[tid~impl~]`.


relation TypeArguments_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`


. If `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the type argument list `[ ]` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Else let `typeArgument~h~ :: typeArgument~t~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `typeArgumentIR~h~` and `tid~impl_h~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArgument_ok, typing `typeArgument~h~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeArgumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl_t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `typeArgument~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl_h~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~impl_t~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Result in the type argument list `typeArgumentIR~h~ :: typeArgumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` and set of fresh type variables `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Sub_expl: `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~`


. Group :
 .. Let `typeIR~a_canon~` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~a~`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR~b_canon~` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~b~`>>.
 .. If <<Sub_expl_canon, `typeIR~a_canon~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b_canon~` after canonicalization>>:
  ... The relation holds.


relation Sub_expl_canon: `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~`


. Group equals:
 .. If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>:
  ... The relation holds.
. Group not-equals:
 .. If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are not the same type>>:
  ... If <<Sub_expl_canon_neq, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~` when they are not the same type after canonicalization>>:
   .... The relation holds.


relation Sub_expl_canon_neq: `typeIR''''''` and `typeIR'''''''`


. If let `primitiveTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
 .. Check that `primitiveTypeIR` matches pattern `BOOL`.
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `BIT < 1 >`.
 .. Group boolean-fixbit:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `numberTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
 .. If `numberTypeIR` matches pattern `INT`:
  ... Group arbint:
   .... If `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `BOOL`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if let `numberTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... If let `INT < _ >` be `numberTypeIR'`:
     ...... The relation holds.
    ..... Else if let `BIT < _ >` be `numberTypeIR'`:
     ...... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `INT < nat >` be `numberTypeIR`:
  ... Let!~type~ `numberTypeIR` be `typeIR'''''''`.
  ... Group fixint:
   .... If `numberTypeIR` matches pattern `INT`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if `numberTypeIR` matches pattern `INT < % >`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Check that `numberTypeIR` is equal to `BIT < nat >`.
   .... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `BIT < nat >` be `numberTypeIR`:
  ... Group fixbit:
   .... If `nat` is equal to 1:
    ..... Check that `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `BOOL`.
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `INT`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `INT < nat >`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if let `numberTypeIR` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... Check that `numberTypeIR` matches pattern `BIT < % >`.
    ..... The relation holds.
. Group newtype:
 .. If let `TYPE _ typeIR~a~` be `typeIR''''''`:
  ... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~a~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR'''''''`>>:
   .... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `TYPE _ typeIR~b~` be `typeIR'''''''`:
  ... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR''''''` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Group serenum:
 .. If let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
  ... Let!~type~ `ENUM _ # typeIR~a~ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`.
  ... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~a~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR'''''''`>>:
   .... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR'''''''`:
  ... Let!~type~ `ENUM _ # typeIR~b~ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`.
  ... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR''''''` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. If let `defaultTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
 .. Group default:
  ... Check that `<<is_defaultable_typeIR, $is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR''''''')>>`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `invalidHeaderTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
 .. Group invalidheader:
  ... If let `HEADER _ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`:
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else if let `HEADER_UNION _ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `sequenceTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
 .. If let `SEQ < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `sequenceTypeIR`:
  ... Group seq:
   .... If let `LIST < typeIR~b~ >` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... If <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... The relation holds.
   .... Else if let `TUPLE < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... If <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... The relation holds.
   .... Else if let `typeIR~b~ [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... Check that the length of `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` is less than or equal to `n~size~`.
    ..... If <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... The relation holds.
   .... Else if let `STRUCT _ { typeIR~b~ _ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... If <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... The relation holds.
   .... Else if let `HEADER _ { typeIR~b~ _ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... If <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... The relation holds.
