for each `typeIR''''^?^` in `typeIR''''^?^^{asterisk}^`
    ..... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~a_aligned~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~b_aligned~`>>, for all `typeIR~a_aligned~` in `typeIR~a_aligned~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b_aligned~` in `typeIR~b_aligned~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... The relation holds.
 .. Else let `RECORD { typeIR~a~ id~a~ ;^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `recordTypeIR`:
  ... Group recorddefault:
   .... If let `STRUCT _ { typeIR~b~ id~b~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... Check that <<sub_set, `{ id~a~^{asterisk}^ }` is a subset of `{ id~b~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR'''^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR'''^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
          * Let `typeIR'''^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<id, typeIR>({ id~a~ : typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ }, id~a~)>>`.
--
+
for each `id~a~` in `id~a~^{asterisk}^`
    ..... Check that `typeIR'''^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR'''^?^` in `typeIR'''^?^^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~a_aligned~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~a_aligned~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
          * Let `?typeIR~a_aligned~` be `typeIR'''^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR'''^?^` in `typeIR'''^?^^{asterisk}^`
    ..... Let `typeIR''''^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR''''^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
          * Let `typeIR''''^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<id, typeIR>({ id~b~ : typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ }, id~a~)>>`.
