+
for each `typeIR'''''^?^` in `typeIR'''''^?^^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Check that `<<is_defaultable_typeIR, $is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR~b_default~)>>`, for all `typeIR~b_default~` in `typeIR~b_default~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... The relation holds.


relation Expr_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `expression'''`


. If let `booleanLiteral` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group literalExpression-boolean:
  ... If `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `TRUE`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BOOL LCTK )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `TRUE # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... Else `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `FALSE`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BOOL LCTK )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `FALSE # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `numberLiteral` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group literalExpression-number:
  ... If let `D i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( INT LCTK )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `D i # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... Else if let `n S i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( INT < n > LCTK )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `n S i # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... Else let `n W i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BIT < n > LCTK )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `n W i # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `" text "` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group literalExpression-stringLiteral:
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( STRING LCTK )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `" text " # expressionNoteIR`.
. Group referenceExpression:
 .. If let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `expression'''`:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `_ typeIR ctk _^?^` be `<<find_var, $find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `prefixedNameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Else if `expression'''` is equal to `THIS`:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `` "this"`.
  ... Let!~option~ `_ typeIR ctk _^?^` be `<<find_var, $find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `prefixedNameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
. If let `defaultExpression` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group defaultExpression:
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( DEFAULT LCTK )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `... # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `unop expression` be `expression'''`:
 .. If `unop` matches pattern `!`:
  ... Group unaryExpression-lnot:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_lnot)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `! typedExpressionIR~reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Else if `unop` matches pattern `~`:
  ... Group unaryExpression-bnot:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_bnot)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `~ typedExpressionIR~reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group unaryExpression-uplusminus:
  ... If `unop` matches pattern `+`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_uplusminus)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `unop typedExpressionIR~reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... Else if `unop` matches pattern `-`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_uplusminus)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `unop typedExpressionIR~reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `expression~l~ binop expression~r~` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group binaryExpression-plusminusmult:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[+, -, *]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_plusminusmult)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-satplusminus:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[|+|, |-|]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_satplusminus)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-divmod:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[/, %]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_divmod)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... If `ctk~r_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~r~)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `n~r~` be `int`.
   .... Check that `n~r~` is greater than 0.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... Else `ctk~r_reduced~` does not match pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-shift:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[<<, >>]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~, $compat_shift)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~l_reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~r_reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Else if `<<is_fixed_bit_typeIR, $is_fixed_bit_typeIR(typeIR~r_reduced~)>>`:
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~l_reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... Else if `ctk~r_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`:
   .... If `<<is_arbitrary_int_typeIR, $is_arbitrary_int_typeIR(typeIR~r_reduced~)>>`:
    ..... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~l_reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... Else if `<<is_fixed_int_typeIR, $is_fixed_int_typeIR(typeIR~r_reduced~)>>`:
    ..... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~l_reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-equality:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[==, !=]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~cast~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_cast~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_cast~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_cast~`>>.
  ... Check that `<<is_equalable_typeIR, $is_equalable_typeIR(typeIR~cast~)>>`.
  ... Let `ctk~cast~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_cast~, ctk~r_cast~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BOOL ctk~cast~ )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_cast~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_cast~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-comparison:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[<=, >=, <, >]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_compare)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BOOL ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-bitwise:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[&, ^, |]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_bitwise)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Check that `binop` matches pattern `++`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-concat:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~, $compat_concat)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~l_reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~r_reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typeIR~reduced~` be `<<result_concat, $result_concat(typeIR~l_reduced~, typeIR~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ ++ typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-logical:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[&&, ||]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_logical)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `expression~cond~ ? expression~true~ : expression~false~` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group ternaryExpression:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR ctk~cond~ )` be `typedExpressionIR~cond~`.
  ... Let!~type~ `primitiveTypeIR` be `typeIR`.
  ... Check that `primitiveTypeIR` matches pattern `BOOL`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~true~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~true~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~false~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~false~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~true_cast~, typedExpressionIR~false_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~true~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~false~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~cast~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~true_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~true_cast~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~true_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~false_cast~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~false_cast~`>>.
  ... Check that `<<is_arbitrary_int_typeIR, $is_arbitrary_int_typeIR(typeIR~cast~)>> => ctk~cond~ =/= DYN`.
  ... Let `ctk` be `<<joins_ctk, $joins_ctk([ctk~cond~, ctk~true_cast~, ctk~false_cast~])>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~cast~ ctk )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~cond~ ? typedExpressionIR~true_cast~ : typedExpressionIR~false_cast~ # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `( type~t~ ) expression` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group castExpression:
  ... Let `typeIR~t~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type~t~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... If <<Type_wf, `typeIR~t~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>`>>:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Let `ctk` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... If <<Sub_expl, `typeIR` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~t~`>>:
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~t~ ctk )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `( typeIR~t~ ) typedExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `dataExpression` be `expression'''`:
 .. If `dataExpression` matches pattern `{#}`:
  ... Group dataExpression-invalid:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( HEADER_INVALID LCTK )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `{#} # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Else let `{ dataElementExpression _ }` be `dataExpression`:
  ... If let `expressionList` be `dataElementExpression`:
   .... Group dataExpression-sequence:
    ..... Let `expression~e~^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_expressionList, the list of expressions in `expressionList`>>.
    ..... If `~... is in expression~e~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... Check that `expression~e~^{asterisk}^` is equal to <<flatten_expressionList, the list of expressions in `expressionList`>>.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~e~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~e~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~e~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `expression~e~` in `expression~e~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~e~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~e~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~e~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e~` in `typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `ctk~e~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~e~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~e~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~e~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e~` in `typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `SEQ < typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^ >`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `<<joins_ctk, $joins_ctk(ctk~e~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `SEQ { typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^ } # expressionNoteIR`.
    ..... Else `...` is in `expression~e~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... Let `expression''^{asterisk}^` be `<<rev_, $rev_<expression>(expression~e~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Let!~type~ `expression' :: expression~e_h_rev~^{asterisk}^` be `expression''^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let!~type~ `defaultExpression` be `expression'`.
     ...... Let `expression~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be `<<rev_, $rev_<expression>(expression~e_h_rev~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Check that `~... is in expression~e_h~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~e_h~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~e_h~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~e_h~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `expression~e_h~` in `expression~e_h~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~e_h~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~e_h~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~e_h~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e_h~` in `typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `ctk~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~e_h~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~e_h~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~e_h~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e_h~` in `typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `SEQ < typeIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^ , ... >`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `<<joins_ctk, $joins_ctk(ctk~e_h~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `SEQ { typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^ , ... } # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... Else let `recordElementExpression` be `dataElementExpression`:
   .... Group dataExpression-record:
    ..... If let `name~f~ = expression~f~` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~` be <<name, the name of `name~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { [typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;] }`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk~f~ )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `RECORD { [nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~] } # expressionNoteIR`.
    ..... Else if let `name~f~ = expression~f~ , ...` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~` be <<name, the name of `name~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { [typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;] , ... }`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk~f~ )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `RECORD { [nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~] , ... } # expressionNoteIR`.
    ..... Else if let `name~f_h~ = expression~f_h~ , namedExpressionList~t~` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `name~f_t~ = expression~f_t~^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_namedExpressionList, the list of named expressions in `namedExpressionList~t~`>>.
     ...... Let `name~f~^{asterisk}^` be `name~f_h~ :: name~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `nameIR~f~` be <<name, the name of `name~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `name~f~` in `name~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `expression~f~^{asterisk}^` be `expression~f_h~ :: expression~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `expression~f~` in `expression~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~f~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `ctk~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `<<joins_ctk, $joins_ctk(ctk~f~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `RECORD { nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^ } # expressionNoteIR`.
    ..... Else let `name~f_h~ = expression~f_h~ , namedExpressionList~t~ , ...` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `name~f_t~ = expression~f_t~^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_namedExpressionList, the list of named expressions in `namedExpressionList~t~`>>.
     ...... Let `name~f~^{asterisk}^` be `name~f_h~ :: name~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `nameIR~f~` be <<name, the name of `name~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `name~f~` in `name~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `expression~f~^{asterisk}^` be `expression~f_h~ :: expression~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `expression~f~` in `expression~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~f~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `ctk~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ , ... }`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `<<joins_ctk, $joins_ctk(ctk~f~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `RECORD { nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^ , ... } # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `ERROR . member` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group errorAccessExpression:
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
  ... Let `nameIR~error~` be `"error." ++ nameIR`.
  ... Check that `ERROR . nameIR` is equal to `<<find_value, $find_value(p, TC, ` nameIR~error~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( ERROR LCTK )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `ERROR . nameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `memberAccessBase . member` be `expression'''`:
 .. If let `prefixedTypeName~base~` be `memberAccessBase`:
  ... Group memberAccessExpression-type:
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR~base~` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName~base~`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `typeDefIR` be `<<find_type, $find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR~base~)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `typeIR~base~` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let!~type~ `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR`.
   .... If let `ENUM _ { nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~base~ LCTK )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `TYPE prefixedNameIR~base~ . nameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... Else let `ENUM _ # _ { nameIR~f~ = _ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~base~ LCTK )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `TYPE prefixedNameIR~base~ . nameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Else let `expression~base~` be `memberAccessBase`:
  ... Group memberAccessExpression-expression:
   .... If `"size"` is equal to <<name, the name of `member`>>:
    ..... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let!~type~ `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BIT < 32 > LCTK )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "size" # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... Else if `"lastIndex"` is equal to <<name, the name of `member`>>:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ <<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let!~type~ `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BIT < 32 > DYN )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "lastIndex" # expressionNoteIR`.
    ..... Else if `p = LOCAL /\ <<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let!~type~ `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BIT < 32 > DYN )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "lastIndex" # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... Else if `"last"` is equal to <<name, the name of `member`>>:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ <<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let!~type~ `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR DYN )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "last" # expressionNoteIR`.
    ..... Else if `p = LOCAL /\ <<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let!~type~ `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR DYN )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "last" # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... Else if `"next"` is equal to <<name, the name of `member`>>:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ <<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let!~type~ `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR DYN )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "next" # expressionNoteIR`.
    ..... Else if `p = LOCAL /\ <<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let!~type~ `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR DYN )`.
     ...... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "next" # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... If let `STRUCT _ { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`:
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
    ..... Let!~option~ `typeIR` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR~f~, typeIR~f~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR DYN )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... Else if let `HEADER _ { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`:
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
    ..... Let!~option~ `typeIR` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR~f~, typeIR~f~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR DYN )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... Else if let `HEADER_UNION _ { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`:
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
    ..... Let!~option~ `typeIR` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR~f~, typeIR~f~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR DYN )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... Else if let `tableMetadataTypeIR` be `typeIR'`:
    ..... Let!~type~ `TABLE_STRUCT _ { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `tableMetadataTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
    ..... Let!~option~ `typeIR` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR~f~, typeIR~f~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR DYN )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `expression~base~ [ expression~index~ ]` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group indexAccessExpression:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~index~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~index~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~base~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~index~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~index~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~index~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~index~`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~index~, $compat_array_index)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... If let `TUPLE < typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'`:
   .... Check that `ctk~index~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
   .... Let `value~index~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~index~)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `n~index~` be `int`.
   .... Check that `n~index~` is less than the length of `typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^[n~index~] DYN )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~ ] # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... Else if let `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`:
   .... If `ctk~index~` matches pattern `LCTK`:
    ..... Let `value~index~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~index~)>>`.
    ..... Let!~type~ `n~index~` be `int`.
    ..... Check that `n~index~` is less than `n~size~`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR DYN )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~ ] # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... Else `ctk~index~` does not match pattern `LCTK`:
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR DYN )`.
    ..... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~ ] # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `expression~base~ [ expression~hi~ : expression~lo~ ]` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group sliceAccessExpression:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~hi~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~hi~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~lo~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~lo~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~base_reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~base~, $compat_bitslice_base)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~base_reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~base_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~base_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~hi~, $compat_bitslice_index)>>`.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~lo~, $compat_bitslice_index)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~hi_reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~hi_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~lo_reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~lo_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`>>.
  ... Check that `ctk~hi_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `value~hi~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~hi~)>>`.
  ... Let!~type~ `n~hi~` be `int`.
  ... Check that `ctk~lo_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `value~lo~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `int'` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~lo~)>>`.
  ... Let!~type~ `n~lo~` be `int'`.
  ... Check that `<<is_valid_bitslice, $is_valid_bitslice(typeIR~base_reduced~, n~lo~, n~hi~)>>`.
  ... Let `int''` be `n~hi~ - n~lo~ + 1`.
  ... Let!~type~ `n~slice~` be `int''`.
  ... Let `typeIR` be `BIT < n~slice~ >`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk~base_reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~ : typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~ ] # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `callExpression` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group callExpression-routine:
  ... If let `callTarget ( argumentList )` be `callExpression`:
   .... Let!~type~ `routineTarget` be `callTarget`.
   .... Let `routineTargetIR` be the result of <<RoutineTarget_ok, typing `routineTarget`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let <<RoutineType_ok, `p TC |- routineTargetIR < [ ] > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : routineTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let <<Call_ok, `p TC |- routineTypeIR < [ ] # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Check that `typeIR~ret~` is not equal to `VOID`.
   .... Let `ctk` be `<<is_static_routineTarget, $is_static_routineTarget(routineTargetIR)>>`.
   .... Let `callExpressionIR` be `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~ret~ ctk )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `callExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... Else let `routineTarget < realTypeArgumentList > ( argumentList )` be `callExpression`:
   .... Let `routineTargetIR` be the result of <<RoutineTarget_ok, typing `routineTarget`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `realTypeArgument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_realTypeArgumentList, the list of real type arguments in `realTypeArgumentList`>>.
   .... Let `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `realTypeArgument^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let <<RoutineType_ok, `p TC |- routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : routineTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let <<Call_ok, `p TC |- routineTypeIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Check that `typeIR~ret~` is not equal to `VOID`.
   .... Let `ctk` be `<<is_static_routineTarget, $is_static_routineTarget(routineTargetIR)>>`.
   .... Let `callExpressionIR` be `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~ret~ ctk )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `callExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Let!~type~ `callTarget ( argumentList )` be `callExpression`.
 .. Group callExpression-constructor:
  ... If let `prefixedTypeName` be `callTarget`:
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
   .... Let <<ConstructorType_ok, `p TC |- prefixedNameIR < [ ] > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let <<Inst_ok, `p TC ANON |- constructorTypeIR < [ ] # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Check that `<<is_concrete_extern_object, $is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR~object~)>>`.
   .... Let `callExpressionIR` be `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~object~ CTK )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `callExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... Else if let `prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList >` be `callTarget`:
   .... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeArgumentList, the list of type arguments in `typeArgumentList`>>.
   .... Let `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
   .... Let <<ConstructorType_ok, `p TC |- prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let <<Inst_ok, `p TC ANON |- constructorTypeIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Check that `<<is_concrete_extern_object, $is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR~object~)>>`.
   .... Let `callExpressionIR` be `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~object~ CTK )`.
   .... Result in the typed expression `callExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR`.
. Else if let `( expression )` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group parenthesizedExpression:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Let `ctk` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
  ... Result in the typed expression `( typedExpressionIR ) # expressionNoteIR`.


relation Argument_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `argument`


. Let!~type~ `expression` be `argument`.
. Group expression:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Result in the typed argument `typedExpressionIR`.
. If let `name = expression` be `argument`:
 .. Group name-expression:
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the typed argument `nameIR = typedExpressionIR`.
. Else if let `name = _` be `argument`:
 .. Group name-dontcare:
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Result in the typed argument `nameIR = _`.
. Else if `argument` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare:
  ... Result in the typed argument `_`.


relation Lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue`


. Let!~type~ `prefixedNonTypeName` be `lvalue`.
. Group referenceExpression-prefixedNonTypeName:
 .. Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
 .. Let!~option~ `direction typeIR ctk value^?^` be `<<find_var, $find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
 .. Check that `ctk` matches pattern `DYN`.
 .. Check that `value^?^` is None.
 .. If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
  ... Result in the typed lvalue `prefixedNameIR # ( typeIR )`.
 .. Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
  ... Result in the typed lvalue `prefixedNameIR # ( typeIR )`.
. If let `lvalue~base~ . member` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group memberAccess:
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ )` be `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... If let `typeIR [ _ ]` be `typeIR'`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... If `nameIR` is equal to `"next"`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ <<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
     ...... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
    ..... Else if `p = LOCAL /\ <<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
     ...... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
   .... Else if `nameIR` is equal to `"last"`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ <<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
     ...... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
    ..... Else if `p = LOCAL /\ <<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
     ...... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
  ... Else if let `STRUCT _ { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `typeIR` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR~f~, typeIR~f~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
   .... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
  ... Else if let `HEADER _ { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `typeIR` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR~f~, typeIR~f~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
   .... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
  ... Else if let `HEADER_UNION _ { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `typeIR` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR~f~, typeIR~f~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
   .... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
. Else if let `lvalue~base~ [ expression~index~ ]` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group indexAccess:
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ )` be `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~index~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~index~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~index~ ctk~index~ )` be `typedExpressionIR~index~`.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~index~, $compat_array_index)>>`.
  ... If `ctk~index~` matches pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `value~index~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~index~)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `n~index~` be `int`.
   .... Check that `n~index~` is less than `n~size~`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~ ] # ( typeIR )`.
   .... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
  ... Else `ctk~index~` does not match pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~ ] # ( typeIR )`.
   .... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
. Else if let `lvalue~base~ [ expression~hi~ : expression~lo~ ]` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group sliceAccess:
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ )` be `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Check that `<<compat_bitslice_base, $compat_bitslice_base(typeIR~base~)>>`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~hi~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~hi~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~lo~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~lo~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~hi~, $compat_bitslice_index)>>`.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~lo~, $compat_bitslice_index)>>`.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~hi_reduced~ ctk~hi_reduced~ )` be `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~lo_reduced~ ctk~lo_reduced~ )` be `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`.
  ... Check that `ctk~hi_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `value~hi~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `int` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~hi~)>>`.
  ... Let!~type~ `n~hi~` be `int`.
  ... Check that `ctk~lo_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `value~lo~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `int'` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~lo~)>>`.
  ... Let!~type~ `n~lo~` be `int'`.
  ... Check that `<<is_valid_bitslice, $is_valid_bitslice(typeIR~base~, n~lo~, n~hi~)>>`.
  ... Let `int''` be `n~hi~ - n~lo~ + 1`.
  ... Let!~type~ `n~slice~` be `int''`.
  ... Let `typeIR` be `BIT < n~slice~ >`.
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~ : typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~ ] # ( typeIR )`.
  ... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
. Else if let `( lvalue~base~ )` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group parenthesized:
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ )` be `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `( typedLvalueIR~base~ ) # ( typeIR~base~ )`.
  ... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.


relation Stmt_ok: `p'`, `TC'`, `f'`, and `statement`


. If let `emptyStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group emptyStatement:
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `;`.
. Else if let `lvalue assignop expression ;` be `statement`:
 .. Check that `assignop` matches pattern `=`.
 .. Group assignmentStatement-eq:
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~l~` be <<type_of_lvalue, the type of lvalue  `typedLvalueIR`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~r~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR`  to  `typeIR~l~`>>.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `typedLvalueIR = typedExpressionIR~cast~ ;`.
. Else if let `callStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group callStatement:
  ... If let `lvalue~routine~ ( argumentList ) ;` be `callStatement`:
   .... Let `routineTargetIR` be the result of <<RoutineTarget_lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~routine~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let <<RoutineType_ok, `p' TC' |- routineTargetIR < [ ] > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : routineTypeIR < # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let <<Call_ok, `p' TC' |- routineTypeIR < [ ] # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `callStatementIR` be `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `callStatementIR`.
  ... Else let `lvalue~routine~ < typeArgumentList > ( argumentList ) ;` be `callStatement`:
   .... Let `routineTargetIR` be the result of <<RoutineTarget_lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~routine~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeArgumentList, the list of type arguments in `typeArgumentList`>>.
   .... Let `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let <<RoutineType_ok, `p' TC' |- routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : routineTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let <<Call_ok, `p' TC' |- routineTypeIR < [ ] # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `callStatementIR` be `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `callStatementIR`.
. Else if let `namedType . APPLY ( argumentList ) ;` be `statement`:
 .. Group directApplicationStatement:
  ... Let `expressionIR # ( typeIR~object~ _ )` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `namedType ( )`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `callExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`.
  ... Let!~type~ `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callExpressionIR`.
  ... Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Check that `<<compat_direct_application, $compat_direct_application(typeIR~object~)>>`.
  ... Let `nameIR~object~` be `"__direct_application"`.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_var, $add_var(p', TC', nameIR~object~, typeIR~object~ CTK ?())>>`.
  ... Let `lvalue` be `nameIR~object~ . "apply"`.
  ... Let `_`, `_`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `lvalue ( argumentList ) ;`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC~1~`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `callStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Let `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR'^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `callStatementIR`.
  ... Check that `routineTargetIR` is equal to `` nameIR~object~ # ( typeIR~object~ CTK ) . "apply"`.
  ... Check that `typeArgumentIR'^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Let `directApplicationStatementIR` be `prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `directApplicationStatementIR`.
. Else if let `exitStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group exitStatement:
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `EXIT ;`.
. Else if let `conditionalStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group conditionalStatement:
  ... If let `IF ( expression~cond~ ) statement~then~` be `conditionalStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~cond~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Check that `BOOL` is equal to <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Let `TC~then~`, `f~then~`, and `statementIR~then~` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement~then~`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC'`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~`.
  ... Else let `IF ( expression~cond~ ) statement~then~ ELSE statement~else~` be `conditionalStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~cond~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Check that `BOOL` is equal to <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Let `TC~then~`, `f~then~`, and `statementIR~then~` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement~then~`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC'`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
   .... Let `TC~else~`, `f~else~`, and `statementIR~else~` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement~else~`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC'`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
   .... Let `f~post~` be <<join_flow, the merged control flow of `f~then~` and `f~else~`>>.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
* and the typed statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~ ELSE statementIR~else~`.
. Check that `p'` matches pattern `LOCAL`.
. If let `returnStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group returnStatement:
  ... If `returnStatement` matches pattern `RETURN ;`:
   .... Check that ?`VOID` is equal to `<<find_return_type, $find_return_type(TC')>>`.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `RET`,
* and the typed statement `RETURN ;`.
  ... Else let `RETURN expression ;` be `returnStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `typeIR~ret~` be `<<find_return_type, $find_return_type(TC')>>`.
   .... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR`  to  `typeIR~ret~`>>.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `RET`,
* and the typed statement `RETURN typedExpressionIR~cast~ ;`.
. Else if let `blockStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group blockStatement:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `f~1~`, and `blockStatementIR` be the result of <<Block_ok, typing `blockStatement`, under typing context `TC'` and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~1~`,
* the abstract control flow `f~1~`,
* and the typed statement `blockStatementIR`.
. Else if let `SWITCH ( expression~switch~ ) { switchCaseList }` be `statement`:
 .. Group switchStatement-table:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~switch~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~switch~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~switch~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~switch~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~switch~`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `tableMetadataTypeIR` be `typeIR`.
  ... Let!~type~ `TABLE_ENUM tid~table_enum~ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `tableMetadataTypeIR`.
  ... Let `tid~table~` be `<<strip_prefix, $strip_prefix(<<strip_suffix, $strip_suffix(tid~table_enum~, ")")>>, "action_list(")>>`.
  ... Let `switchCase^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_switchCaseList, the list of switch cases in `switchCaseList`>>.
  ... Let <<SwitchCases_table_ok, `TC' f' tid~table~ |- switchCase^{asterisk}^ : f~post~ switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `switchLabel^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... Let `switchStatementIR` be `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR~switch~ ) { switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
* and the typed statement `switchStatementIR`.
 .. Group switchStatement-general:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~switch~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~switch~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~switch~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~switch~`>>.
  ... Check that `<<compat_switch, $compat_switch(typeIR~switch~)>>`.
  ... Let `switchCase^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_switchCaseList, the list of switch cases in `switchCaseList`>>.
  ... Let <<SwitchCases_general_ok, `TC' f' typeIR~switch~ |- switchCase^{asterisk}^ : f~post~ switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `switchLabel^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... Let `switchStatementIR` be `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR~switch~ ) { switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
* and the typed statement `switchStatementIR`.


relation BlockElementStmt_ok: `TC~0~`, `f`, and `blockElementStatement`


. If let `constantDeclaration` be `blockElementStatement`:
 .. Group constantDeclaration:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `constantDeclaration`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`,
* and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `constantDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~1~`,
* the abstract control flow `f`,
* and the typed block element statement `constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList type name initializerOpt ;` be `blockElementStatement`:
 .. Group variableDeclaration:
  ... If `initializerOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... If <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(LOCAL, TC~0~)>>`>>:
    ..... Check that `<<is_assignable_typeIR, $is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
    ..... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_var, $add_var(LOCAL, TC~0~, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())>>`.
    ..... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR ?() ;`.
    ..... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~1~`,
* the abstract control flow `f`,
* and the typed block element statement `variableDeclarationIR`.
  ... Else if let `= expression~init~` be `initializerOpt`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... If <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(LOCAL, TC~0~)>>`>>:
    ..... Check that `<<is_assignable_typeIR, $is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
    ..... Let `typedExpressionIR~init~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~init~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
    ..... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~init_cast~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~init~`  to  `typeIR`>>.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
    ..... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_var, $add_var(LOCAL, TC~0~, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())>>`.
    ..... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR ?= typedExpressionIR~init_cast~ ;`.
    ..... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~1~`,
* the abstract control flow `f`,
* and the typed block element statement `variableDeclarationIR`.
. Else let `statement` be `blockElementStatement`:
 .. Group statement:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `f~post~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0~`, and abstract control flow `f`>>.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~1~`,
* the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
* and the typed block element statement `statementIR`.


relation BlockElementStmts_ok: `TC'`, `f'`, and `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^`


. If `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed block element statements `[ ]`.
. Else let `blockElementStatement~h~ :: blockElementStatement~t~^{asterisk}^` be `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `f~1~`, and `blockElementStatementIR~h~` be the result of <<BlockElementStmt_ok, typing `blockElementStatement~h~`, under typing context `TC'` and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~`, `f~2~`, and `blockElementStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<BlockElementStmts_ok, typing `blockElementStatement~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~` and abstract control flow `f~1~`>>.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~2~`,
* the abstract control flow `f~2~`,
* and the typed block element statements `blockElementStatementIR~h~ :: blockElementStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Block_ok: `TC~0~`, `f`, and `annotationList { blockElementStatementList }`


. Group :
 .. Let `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_blockElementStatementList, the list of block element statements in `blockElementStatementList`>>.
 .. Let `TC~1~` be `<<enter, $enter(TC~0~)>>`.
 .. Let `TC~2~`, `f~post~`, and `blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<BlockElementStmts_ok, typing `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~` and abstract control flow `f`>>.
 .. Let `TC~3~` be `<<exit, $exit(TC~2~)>>`.
 .. Let `blockStatementIR` be `annotationList { blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
 .. Result in 
* the typing context `TC~3~`,
* the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
* and the typed block statement `blockStatementIR`.


relation Parameter_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `annotationList direction type name initializerOpt`


. Group :
 .. If `initializerOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `bound` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>` and `{ tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
  ... If <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Result in the parameter `annotationList direction typeIR nameIR ?()` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Else if let `= expression~init~` be `initializerOpt`:
  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `bound` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>` and `{ tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
  ... If <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~init~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~init~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~init~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~init~`>>.
   .... Check that `<<ctk_of_expression, $ctk_of_expression(typedExpressionIR~init~)>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
   .... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~init_cast~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~init~`  to  `typeIR`>>.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `value~init~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~init_cast~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Result in the parameter `annotationList direction typeIR nameIR ?= value~init~` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Parameters_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `parameter^{asterisk}^`


. If `parameter^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the parameter list `[ ]` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Else let `parameter~h~ :: parameter~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parameter^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `parameterIR~h~` and `tid~fresh_h~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameter_ok, typing `parameter~h~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `parameterIR~t~^{asterisk}^` and `tid~fresh_t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the parameter list `parameterIR~h~ :: parameterIR~t~^{asterisk}^` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh_h~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~fresh_t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ConstructorParameter_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `constructorParameter`


. Group :
 .. Let `constructorParameterIR` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameter_ok, typing `constructorParameter`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Result in the constructor parameter `constructorParameterIR` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ConstructorParameters_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `constructorParameter^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. Let `constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `constructorParameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Result in the constructor parameter list `constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ExternMethod_ok: `TC~0~`, `tid~extern~`, and `externMethodPrototype`


. If let `annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) ;` be `externMethodPrototype`:
 .. Group non-abstract:
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Check that `nameIR` is not equal to `tid~extern~`.
  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeParameterListOpt, the list of type parameters in `typeParameterListOpt`>>.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be <<name, the name of `typeParameter`>>.
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_types, $add_types(LOCAL, TC~0~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, TID tid~expl~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~ret~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `typeOrVoid`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `TC~1~`[LOCAL.KIND = `EXTERN_METHOD -> typeIR~ret~`].
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parameterList, the list of parameters in `parameterList`>>.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~2~`>>.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `<<add_parameters, $add_parameters(LOCAL, TC~2~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `rid` be `<<rid, $rid(name, parameterList)>>`.
  ... Let `methodTypeIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `methodTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
  ... If <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `routineTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(BLOCK, TC~0~)>>`>>:
   .... Let `TC~4~` be `<<add_routine_overload, $add_routine_overload(BLOCK, TC~0~, rid, routineTypeDefIR)>>`.
   .... Let `externMethodPrototypeIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
   .... Result in the updated typing context `TC~4~` and the typed method prototype `externMethodPrototypeIR`.
. Else let `annotationList ABSTRACT typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) ;` be `externMethodPrototype`:
 .. Group abstract:
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Check that `nameIR` is not equal to `tid~extern~`.
  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeParameterListOpt, the list of type parameters in `typeParameterListOpt`>>.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be <<name, the name of `typeParameter`>>.
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_types, $add_types(LOCAL, TC~0~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, TID tid~expl~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~ret~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `typeOrVoid`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `TC~1~`[LOCAL.KIND = `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT -> typeIR~ret~`].
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parameterList, the list of parameters in `parameterList`>>.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~2~`>>.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `<<add_parameters, $add_parameters(LOCAL, TC~2~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `rid` be `<<rid, $rid(name, parameterList)>>`.
  ... Let `methodTypeIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `methodTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
  ... If <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `routineTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(BLOCK, TC~0~)>>`>>:
   .... Let `TC~4~` be `<<add_routine_overload, $add_routine_overload(BLOCK, TC~0~, rid, routineTypeDefIR)>>`.
   .... Let `externMethodPrototypeIR` be `annotationList ABSTRACT typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
   .... Result in the updated typing context `TC~4~` and the typed method prototype `externMethodPrototypeIR`.


relation ExternMethods_ok: `TC'`, `tid~extern~`, and `externMethodPrototype^{asterisk}^`


. If `externMethodPrototype^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC'` and the typed method prototypes `[ ]`.
. Else let `externMethodPrototype~h~ :: externMethodPrototype~t~^{asterisk}^` be `externMethodPrototype^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `externMethodPrototypeIR~h~` be the result of <<ExternMethod_ok, typing `externMethodPrototype~h~`, under typing context `TC'` for an extern object `tid~extern~`>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `externMethodPrototypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ExternMethods_ok, typing `externMethodPrototype~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~` for an extern object `tid~extern~`>>.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~2~` and the typed method prototypes `externMethodPrototypeIR~h~ :: externMethodPrototypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ExternConstructor_ok: `TC~0~`, `tid~extern~`, and `annotationList typeIdentifier ( parameterList ) ;`


. Group :
 .. Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `typeIdentifier`>>.
 .. Check that `nameIR` is equal to `tid~extern~`.
 .. Let `constructorParameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parameterList, the list of parameters in `parameterList`>>.
 .. Let `constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ConstructorParameters_ok, typing `constructorParameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
 .. Let `constructorParameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `constructorParameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `constructorParameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_constructorParameterIR, the type of  `constructorParameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `constructorParameterIR` in `constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let!~option~ `typeDefIR` be `<<find_type, $find_type(GLOBAL, TC~0~, ` nameIR)>>`.
 .. Let!~type~ `typeIR~extern~ < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeDefIR`.
 .. Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Let `cid` be `<<cid, $cid(typeIdentifier, ( parameterList ))>>`.
 .. Let `typeIR~extern_spec~` be `typeIR~extern~ < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , [ ] > < TID tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
 .. Let `constructorTypeIR` be `CONSTRUCTOR ( constructorParameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~extern_spec~`.
 .. Let `constructorTypeDefIR` be `constructorTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
 .. If <<ConstructorTypeDef_wf, `constructorTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(BLOCK, TC~0~)>>`>>:
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_constructor, $add_constructor(TC~0~, cid, constructorTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Let `externConstructorPrototypeIR` be `annotationList nameIR < , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed constructor prototype `externConstructorPrototypeIR`.


relation ExternConstructors_ok: `TC'`, `tid~extern~`, and `externConstructorPrototype^{asterisk}^`


. If `externConstructorPrototype^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC'` and the typed constructor prototypes `[ ]`.
. Else let `externConstructorPrototype~h~ :: externConstructorPrototype~t~^{asterisk}^` be `externConstructorPrototype^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `externConstructorPrototypeIR~h~` be the result of <<ExternConstructor_ok, typing `externConstructorPrototype~h~`, under typing context `TC'` for an extern object `tid~extern~`>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `externConstructorPrototypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ExternConstructors_ok, typing `externConstructorPrototype~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~` for an extern object `tid~extern~`>>.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~2~` and the typed constructor prototypes `externConstructorPrototypeIR~h~ :: externConstructorPrototypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ParserTransition_ok: `TC~0~`, `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`, and `transitionStatement`


. If `transitionStatement` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
 .. Group empty:
  ... Result in the typed transition statement `TRANSITION "reject" ;`.
. Else let `TRANSITION stateExpression` be `transitionStatement`:
 .. Else if let `name ;` be `stateExpression`:
  ... Group name:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `transitionStatementIR` be `TRANSITION nameIR ;`.
   .... Result in the typed transition statement `transitionStatementIR`.
 .. Else if let `SELECT ( expressionList~key~ ) { selectCaseList }` be `stateExpression`:
  ... Group switch:
   .... Let `expression~key~^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_expressionList, the list of expressions in `expressionList~key~`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~key~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~key~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `typedExpressionIR~key~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~key~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
--
+
for each `expression~key~` in `expression~key~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~key~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `typeIR~key~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~key~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~key~` in `typedExpressionIR~key~^{asterisk}^`
   .... If <<Type_wf, `SET < [typeIR~key~] >` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(LOCAL, TC~0~)>>`>>, for all `typeIR~key~` in `typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... Let `selectCase^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_selectCaseList, the list of select cases in `selectCaseList`>>.
    ..... Let `selectCaseIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `selectCaseIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
          * Let <<SelectCase_ok, `TC~0~ nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^ typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^ |- selectCase : selectCaseIR`>>.
--
+
for each `selectCase` in `selectCase^{asterisk}^`
    ..... Let `transitionStatementIR` be `TRANSITION SELECT ( typedExpressionIR~key~^{asterisk}^ ) { selectCaseIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
    ..... Result in the typed transition statement `transitionStatementIR`.


relation ParserStmt_ok: `TC~0'~` and `parserStatement''`


. If let `constantDeclaration` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group constantDeclaration:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `constantDeclaration`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0'~`,
* and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `constantDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList type name initializerOpt ;` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group variableDeclaration:
  ... If `initializerOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... If <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(LOCAL, TC~0'~)>>`>>:
    ..... Check that `<<is_assignable_typeIR, $is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
    ..... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_var, $add_var(LOCAL, TC~0'~, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())>>`.
    ..... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR ?() ;`.
    ..... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `variableDeclarationIR`.
  ... Else if let `= expression~init~` be `initializerOpt`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... If <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(LOCAL, TC~0'~)>>`>>:
    ..... Check that `<<is_assignable_typeIR, $is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
    ..... Let `typedExpressionIR~init~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~init~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
    ..... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~init_cast~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~init~`  to  `typeIR`>>.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
    ..... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_var, $add_var(LOCAL, TC~0'~, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())>>`.
    ..... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR ?= typedExpressionIR~init_cast~ ;`.
    ..... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `variableDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `emptyStatement` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group emptyStatement:
  ... Let `typingContext`, `flow`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `emptyStatement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0'~`, and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Check that `typingContext` is equal to `TC~0'~`.
  ... Check that `flow` matches pattern `CONT`.
  ... Let!~type~ `emptyStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~0'~` and the typed parser statement `emptyStatementIR`.
. Else if let `assignmentStatement` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group assignmentStatement:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `flow`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `assignmentStatement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0'~`, and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Check that `flow` matches pattern `CONT`.
  ... Let!~type~ `assignmentStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `assignmentStatementIR`.
. Else if let `callStatement` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group callStatement:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `flow`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `callStatement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0'~`, and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Check that `flow` matches pattern `CONT`.
  ... Let!~type~ `callStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `callStatementIR`.
. Else if let `directApplicationStatement` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group directApplicationStatement:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `flow`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `directApplicationStatement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0'~`, and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Check that `flow` matches pattern `CONT`.
  ... Let!~type~ `directApplicationStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `directApplicationStatementIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList { parserStatementList }` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group parserBlockStatement:
  ... Let `parserStatement^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parserStatementList, the list of parser statements in `parserStatementList`>>.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `<<enter, $enter(TC~0'~)>>`.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ParserStmts_ok, typing `parserStatement^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `<<exit, $exit(TC~2~)>>`.
  ... Let `parserBlockStatementIR` be `annotationList { parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `parserBlockStatementIR`.
. Else let `conditionalStatement` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group conditionalStatement:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `flow`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `conditionalStatement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0'~`, and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Check that `flow` matches pattern `CONT`.
  ... Let!~type~ `conditionalStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `conditionalStatementIR`.


relation ParserStmts_ok: `TC'` and `parserStatement^{asterisk}^`


. If `parserStatement^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC'` and the typed parser statements `[ ]`.
. Else let `parserStatement~h~ :: parserStatement~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parserStatement^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `parserStatementIR~h~` be the result of <<ParserStmt_ok, typing `parserStatement~h~`, under typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `parserStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ParserStmts_ok, typing `parserStatement~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~2~` and the typed parser statements `parserStatementIR~h~ :: parserStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ParserState_ok: `TC~0~`, `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`, and `annotationList STATE name { parserStatementList transitionStatement }`


. Group :
 .. Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
 .. Let `TC~1~` be `<<enter, $enter(TC~0~)>>`.
 .. Let `parserStatement^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parserStatementList, the list of parser statements in `parserStatementList`>>.
 .. Let `TC~2~` and `parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ParserStmts_ok, typing `parserStatement^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~`>>.
 .. Let `transitionStatementIR` be the result of <<ParserTransition_ok, typing `transitionStatement`, under typing context `TC~2~` and parser state names `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`>>.
 .. Let `TC~3~` be `<<exit, $exit(TC~2~)>>`.
 .. Let `parserStateIR` be `annotationList STATE nameIR { parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^ transitionStatementIR }`.
 .. Result in the typed parser state `parserStateIR`.


relation ParserStates_ok: `TC` and `parserState^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. Let `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, and `name~state~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `name~state~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `_ STATE name~state~ { _ _ }` be `parserState`.
--
+
for each `parserState` in `parserState^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~state~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `nameIR~state~` be <<name, the name of `name~state~`>>.
--
+
for each `name~state~` in `name~state~^{asterisk}^`
 .. Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
 .. Check that `"start"` is in `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `~"accept" is in nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^ /\ ~"reject" is in nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `nameIR~state_impl~^{asterisk}^` be `"accept" :: "reject" :: nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parserStateIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parserStateIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `parserStateIR` be the result of <<ParserState_ok, typing `parserState`, under typing context `TC` and parser state names `nameIR~state_impl~^{asterisk}^`>>.
--
+
for each `parserState` in `parserState^{asterisk}^`
 .. Result in the typed parser states `parserStateIR^{asterisk}^`.


