. Else if let `enumTypeDeclaration` be `declaration`:
 .. If let `annotationList ENUM name { nameList~field~ _ }` be `enumTypeDeclaration`:
  ... Group enumTypeDeclaration-non-serializable:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `name~field~^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_nameList, the list of names in `nameList~field~`>>.
   .... Let `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `nameIR~field~` be <<name, the name of `name~field~`>>.
--
+
for each `name~field~` in `name~field~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `typeIR~enum~` be `ENUM nameIR { nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^ }`.
   .... If <<TypeDef_wf, `typeIR~enum~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(GLOBAL, TC~0~)>>`>>:
    ..... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_type, $add_type(GLOBAL, TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~enum~)>>`.
    ..... Let `id~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `id~field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
          * Let `id~field~` be `nameIR ++ "." ++ nameIR~field~`.
