relation Decls_ok: `p`, `TC'`, and `declaration^{asterisk}^`


. If `declaration^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the modified typing context `TC'` and the typed declarations `[ ]`.
. Else let `declaration~h~ :: declaration~t~^{asterisk}^` be `declaration^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR~h~` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `declaration~h~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC'`,
* and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_ok, typing `declaration~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC~1~`,
* and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Result in the modified typing context `TC~2~` and the typed declarations `declarationIR~h~ :: declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Program_ok: `p4program`


. Group :
 .. Let `declaration^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_p4program, the list of declarations in `p4program`>>.
 .. Let `TC~0~` be `<<empty_typingContext, $empty_typingContext>>`.
 .. Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_ok, typing `declaration^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `GLOBAL` and typing context `TC~0~`,
* and the modified typing context>>.
 .. Result in the typing context `TC~1~` and the typed P4 program `declarationIR^{asterisk}^ ;`.


relation Call_convention_expr_ok: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `direction typeIR~param~ _ _^?^`, and `typedExpressionIR~arg~`


. If `direction` matches pattern `IN`:
 .. Group in:
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`  to  `typeIR~param~`>>.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`.
. Group out-inout:
 .. If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>:
   .... If <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>:
    ..... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.
 .. Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
  ... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>:
   .... If <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>:
    ..... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.
. Else if `direction` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
 .. Group empty:
  ... If `actctxt` matches pattern `ACTION`:
   .... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`  to  `typeIR~param~`>>.
   .... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`.
  ... Else `actctxt` matches pattern `NOACTION`:
   .... Let `typeIR~arg~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~arg~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
   .... If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>:
    ..... Check that `ctk~arg~` does not match pattern `DYN`.
    ..... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.


relation Call_convention_argument_ok: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR`, and `argumentIR`


. Let!~type~ `typedExpressionIR` be `argumentIR`.
. Group typedExpression:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be the result of <<Call_convention_expr_ok, checking the calling convention of `typedExpressionIR` applied to parameter type `parameterTypeIR`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `actctxt`>>.
 .. Result in `typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. If let `nameIR = typedExpressionIR` be `argumentIR`:
 .. Group nameIR-typedExpression:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be the result of <<Call_convention_expr_ok, checking the calling convention of `typedExpressionIR` applied to parameter type `parameterTypeIR`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `actctxt`>>.
  ... Result in `nameIR = typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. Else if let `nameIR = _` be `argumentIR`:
 .. Group nameIR-dontcare:
  ... Let `direction _ _ _^?^` be `parameterTypeIR`.
  ... Check that `direction` matches pattern `OUT`.
  ... Result in `nameIR = _`.
. Else if `argumentIR` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare:
  ... Let `direction _ _ _^?^` be `parameterTypeIR`.
  ... Check that `direction` matches pattern `OUT`.
  ... Result in `_`.


relation Call_convention_ok: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `[ ]`.
. Else let `parameterTypeIR~h~ :: parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Let!~type~ `argumentIR~h~ :: argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `argumentIR~h_cast~` be the result of <<Call_convention_argument_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR~h~` applied to parameter type `parameterTypeIR~h~`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `actctxt`>>.
  ... Let `argumentIR~t_cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `actctxt`>>.
  ... Result in `argumentIR~h_cast~ :: argumentIR~t_cast~^{asterisk}^`.


relation RoutineTarget_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `routineTarget`


. Group referenceExpression:
 .. If let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `routineTarget`:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Check that `prefixedNameIR = ` "verify" \/ prefixedNameIR = . "verify" => p = BLOCK /\ <<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>> \/ p = LOCAL /\ <<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`.
  ... Result in the typed routine target `prefixedNameIR`.
 .. Else if `routineTarget` is equal to `THIS`:
  ... Result in the typed routine target `` "this"`.
. If let `memberAccessBase . member` be `routineTarget`:
 .. Group memberAccessExpression:
  ... If let `prefixedTypeName` be `memberAccessBase`:
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Result in the typed routine target `TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR`.
  ... Else let `expression~base~` be `memberAccessBase`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Result in the typed routine target `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR`.
. Else if let `( expression )` be `routineTarget`:
 .. Group parenthesizedExpression:
  ... Let `routineTargetIR` be the result of <<RoutineTarget_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the typed routine target `( routineTargetIR )`.


relation RoutineTarget_lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue`


. Group :
 .. Let `expression` be <<lvalue_as_expression, the expression corresponding to `lvalue`>>.
 .. Let `routineTargetIR` be the result of <<RoutineTarget_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Result in the typed routine target `routineTargetIR`.


relation RoutineType_ok: `p`, `TC`, `routineTargetIR''`, `typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^`


. Let!~type~ `prefixedNameIR` be `routineTargetIR''`.
. Group referenceExpressionIR:
 .. If `typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`:
  ... Let!~option~ `(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)` be `<<find_routine_overloaded, $find_routine_overloaded(p, TC, prefixedNameIR, argumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let!~type~ `(rid, actionTypeIR, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)`.
  ... If <<RoutineType_wf, `actionTypeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>`>>:
   .... Result in `actionTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)^?^` be `<<find_routine_overloaded, $find_routine_overloaded(p, TC, prefixedNameIR, argumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Else if let `?(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)^?^`:
  ... Let `(routineTypeDefIR, tid*)` be `<<specialize_routineTypeDef, $specialize_routineTypeDef(routineTypeDefIR, typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let!~type~ `(functionTypeIR, tid~impl~^{asterisk}^)` be `(routineTypeDefIR, tid*)`.
  ... Let `bound` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>` and `{ tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
  ... If <<RoutineType_wf, `functionTypeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>:
   .... Result in `functionTypeIR`, `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.
. If let `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR` be `routineTargetIR''`:
 .. Else if `typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
  ... If `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-minmax-SizeIn-BitsBytes:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
    ..... Let `methodTypeIR` be `BUILTIN_METHOD ( [ ] ) -> INT`.
    ..... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-header-isValid:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["isValid"]`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let!~type~ `HEADER _ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR`.
    ..... Let `methodTypeIR` be `BUILTIN_METHOD ( [ ] ) -> BOOL`.
    ..... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-union-isValid:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["isValid"]`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let!~type~ `HEADER_UNION _ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR`.
    ..... Let `methodTypeIR` be `BUILTIN_METHOD ( [ ] ) -> BOOL`.
    ..... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-header-set-ValidInvalid:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["setValid", "setInvalid"]`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let!~type~ `HEADER _ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR`.
    ..... Let `methodTypeIR` be `BUILTIN_METHOD ( [ ] ) -> VOID`.
    ..... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
  ... Else if let `[argumentIR]` be `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^`:
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-stack-push-pop-front:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["push_front", "pop_front"]`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let!~type~ `typeIR [ _ ]` be `typeIR'`.
    ..... Let `parameterTypeIR` be `INT "count" ?()`.
    ..... Let `methodTypeIR` be `BUILTIN_METHOD ( [parameterTypeIR] ) -> INT`.
    ..... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
 .. Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-extern-method:
  ... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `EXTERN _ { rid~f~ : routineTypeDefIR~f~^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR`.
  ... Let `id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^` be `<<ids_arguments, $ids_arguments(argumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let!~option~ `(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<find_overloaded, $find_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>({ rid~f~ : routineTypeDefIR~f~^{asterisk}^ }, nameIR, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `(routineTypeDefIR, tid*)` be `<<specialize_routineTypeDef, $specialize_routineTypeDef(routineTypeDefIR, typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let!~type~ `(routineTypeIR, tid~impl~^{asterisk}^)` be `(routineTypeDefIR, tid*)`.
  ... Let `bound` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>` and `{ tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
  ... If <<RoutineType_wf, `routineTypeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>:
   .... Result in `routineTypeIR`, `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Else if `nameIR` is equal to `"apply"`:
  ... Check that `typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-parser-apply-method:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let!~type~ `PARSER ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR` be `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `id~param~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `id~param~`, and `value~param~^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~param~^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `_ _ id~param~ value~param~^?^` be `parameterTypeIR`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR` in `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `pid^{asterisk}^` be the list of `pid`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `pid` be `id~param~ # value~param~^?^ =/= ?()`.
--
+
for each `id~param~` in `id~param~^{asterisk}^` and `value~param~^?^` in `value~param~^?^^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `rid` be `"apply" ( pid^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^` be `<<ids_arguments, $ids_arguments(argumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let!~option~ `(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)` be `<<find_overloaded, $find_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>({ [rid : methodTypeIR] }, "apply", id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `(rid', methodTypeIR', id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)`.
   .... Check that `rid'` is equal to `rid`.
   .... Check that `methodTypeIR'` is equal to `methodTypeIR`.
   .... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-control-apply-method:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let!~type~ `CONTROL ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR` be `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `id~param~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `id~param~`, and `value~param~^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~param~^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `_ _ id~param~ value~param~^?^` be `parameterTypeIR`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR` in `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `pid^{asterisk}^` be the list of `pid`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `pid` be `id~param~ # value~param~^?^ =/= ?()`.
--
+
for each `id~param~` in `id~param~^{asterisk}^` and `value~param~^?^` in `value~param~^?^^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `rid` be `"apply" ( pid^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^` be `<<ids_arguments, $ids_arguments(argumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let!~option~ `(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)` be `<<find_overloaded, $find_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>({ [rid : methodTypeIR] }, "apply", id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `(rid', methodTypeIR', id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)`.
   .... Check that `rid'` is equal to `rid`.
   .... Check that `methodTypeIR'` is equal to `methodTypeIR`.
   .... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-table-apply-method:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let!~type~ `TABLE _ # typeIR~table~` be `typeIR`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR` be `TABLE_APPLY -> typeIR~table~`.
   .... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
. Else if let `( routineTargetIR )` be `routineTargetIR''`:
 .. Group parenthesized:
  ... Let <<RoutineType_ok, `p TC |- routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR''^{asterisk}^ ) : routineTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
  ... Result in `routineTypeIR`, `tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Call_ok: `p`, `TC`, `routineTypeIR`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^`, `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default'~^{asterisk}^`


. If let `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Group function:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameters, $filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameters, $align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `inference` be `<<infer, $infer(tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `typeIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid~infer'~)>>`.
--
+
for each `tid~infer'~` in `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Check that `typeIR^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `?typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ ++ typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `<<subst_parameterType, $subst_parameterType(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)>>`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeIR~ret_inferred~` be `<<subst_type, $subst_type(inference, typeIR~ret~)>>`.
  ... Let `functionTypeIR~inferred~` be `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_inferred~`.
  ... If <<RoutineType_wf, `functionTypeIR~inferred~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>`>>:
   .... Check that `<<callable_function, $callable_function(p, TC)>>`.
   .... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
   .... Result in `typeIR~ret_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Group externfunction:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameters, $filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameters, $align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `inference` be `<<infer, $infer(tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `typeIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid~infer'~)>>`.
--
+
for each `tid~infer'~` in `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Check that `typeIR^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `?typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ ++ typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `<<subst_parameterType, $subst_parameterType(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)>>`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeIR~ret_inferred~` be `<<subst_type, $subst_type(inference, typeIR~ret~)>>`.
  ... Let `functionTypeIR~inferred~` be `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_inferred~`.
  ... If <<RoutineType_wf, `functionTypeIR~inferred~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>`>>:
   .... Check that `<<callable_extern_function, $callable_extern_function(p, TC)>>`.
   .... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
   .... Result in `typeIR~ret_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Check that `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group action:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameters, $filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameters, $align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that `<<callable_action, $callable_action(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `ACTION`>>.
  ... Result in `VOID`, `[ ]`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `BUILTIN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group builtin-method:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameters, $filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameters, $align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that `<<callable_builtin_method, $callable_builtin_method(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
  ... Result in `typeIR~ret~`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `externMethodTypeIR` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. If let `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~` be `externMethodTypeIR`:
  ... Group extern-method:
   .... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameters, $filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameters, $align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `inference` be `<<infer, $infer(tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `typeIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid~infer'~)>>`.
--
+
for each `tid~infer'~` in `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Check that `typeIR^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `?typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ ++ typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `<<subst_parameterType, $subst_parameterType(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)>>`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `typeIR~ret_inferred~` be `<<subst_type, $subst_type(inference, typeIR~ret~)>>`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR~inferred~` be `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_inferred~`.
   .... If <<RoutineType_wf, `methodTypeIR~inferred~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>`>>:
    ..... Check that `<<callable_extern_method, $callable_extern_method(p, TC)>>`.
    ..... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
    ..... Result in `typeIR~ret_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Else let `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~` be `externMethodTypeIR`:
  ... Group extern-abstract-method:
   .... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameters, $filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameters, $align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `inference` be `<<infer, $infer(tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `typeIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid~infer'~)>>`.
--
+
for each `tid~infer'~` in `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Check that `typeIR^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `?typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ ++ typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `<<subst_parameterType, $subst_parameterType(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)>>`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `typeIR~ret_inferred~` be `<<subst_type, $subst_type(inference, typeIR~ret~)>>`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR~inferred~` be `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_inferred~`.
   .... If <<RoutineType_wf, `methodTypeIR~inferred~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>`>>:
    ..... Check that `<<callable_extern_abstract_method, $callable_extern_abstract_method(p, TC)>>`.
    ..... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
    ..... Result in `typeIR~ret_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Check that `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group parser-apply-method:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameters, $filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameters, $align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that `<<callable_parser_apply_method, $callable_parser_apply_method(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
  ... Result in `VOID`, `[ ]`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Check that `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group control-apply-method:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameters, $filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameters, $align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that `<<callable_control_apply_method, $callable_control_apply_method(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
  ... Result in `VOID`, `[ ]`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else let `TABLE_APPLY -> typeIR~table~` be `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Check that `tid~infer'~^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Check that `id~default'~^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group table-apply-method:
  ... Check that `<<callable_table_apply_method, $callable_table_apply_method(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Result in `typeIR~table~`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.


relation ConstructorType_ok: `p`, `TC`, `prefixedNameIR`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. Let!~option~ `(cid, constructorTypeDefIR, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<find_constructor_overloaded, $find_constructor_overloaded(TC, prefixedNameIR, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `(constructorTypeIR, tid~impl~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<specialize_constructorTypeDef, $specialize_constructorTypeDef(constructorTypeDefIR, typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `bound` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>` and `{ tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
 .. If <<ConstructorType_wf, `constructorTypeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>:
  ... Result in `constructorTypeIR`, `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Inst_ok: `cursor'`, `TC`, `instctxt`, `constructorTypeIR`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`, `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`


. Check that `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`.
. Group package:
 .. Let `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~object~` be `constructorTypeIR`.
 .. Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~object~`>>.
 .. Let!~type~ `PACKAGE < _^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameters, $filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameters, $align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `inference` be `<<infer, $infer(tid~infer~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `typeIR'^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR'^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR'^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid~infer~)>>`.
--
+
for each `tid~infer~` in `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`
 .. Check that `typeIR'^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR'^?^` in `typeIR'^?^^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `?typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR'^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR'^?^` in `typeIR'^?^^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ ++ typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `<<subst_parameterType, $subst_parameterType(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)>>`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `typeIR~object_inferred~` be `<<subst_type, $subst_type(inference, typeIR~object~)>>`.
 .. Let `constructorTypeIR~inferred~` be `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~object_inferred~`.
 .. If <<ConstructorType_wf, `constructorTypeIR~inferred~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(GLOBAL, TC)>>`>>:
  ... Check that `<<instantiable, $instantiable(GLOBAL, TC, instctxt, typeIR~object_inferred~)>>`.
  ... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `BLOCK`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
  ... Result in `typeIR~object_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Group non-package:
 .. Let `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~object~` be `constructorTypeIR`.
 .. Check that `~<<is_package_object_typeIR, $is_package_object_typeIR(<<canon, $canon(typeIR~object~)>>)>>`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameters, $filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameters, $align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `inference` be `<<infer, $infer(tid~infer~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid~infer~)>>`.
--
+
for each `tid~infer~` in `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`
 .. Check that `typeIR^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `?typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ ++ typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `<<subst_parameterType, $subst_parameterType(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)>>`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `typeIR~object_inferred~` be `<<subst_type, $subst_type(inference, typeIR~object~)>>`.
 .. Let `constructorTypeIR~inferred~` be `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~object_inferred~`.
 .. If <<ConstructorType_wf, `constructorTypeIR~inferred~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(cursor', TC)>>`>>:
  ... Check that `<<instantiable, $instantiable(cursor', TC, instctxt, typeIR~object_inferred~)>>`.
  ... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `cursor'`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
  ... Result in `typeIR~object_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.


relation SwitchLabel_table_ok: `TC`, `tid~table~`, `bool`, and `switchLabel`


. Group :
 .. If `bool` is equal to true:
  ... Check that `switchLabel` matches pattern `DEFAULT`.
  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.
 .. Else if let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `switchLabel`:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `` nameIR~label~` be `prefixedNameIR`.
  ... Let `tid~table_enum~` be `"action_list(" ++ tid~table~ ++ ")"`.
  ... Let `id~label~` be `tid~table_enum~ ++ "." ++ nameIR~label~`.
  ... Let!~option~ `_ typeIR~label~ ctk~label~ value^?^` be `<<find_var, $find_var(LOCAL, TC, ` id~label~)>>`.
  ... Let!~type~ `?value~label~` be `value^?^`.
  ... Check that `value~label~` is equal to `TABLE_ENUM tid~table_enum~ . nameIR~label~`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~label~` be `` nameIR~label~ # ( typeIR~label~ ctk~label~ )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~label~`.


relation SwitchCase_table_ok: `TC`, `f`, `tid~table~`, `b~last~`, and `switchCase`


. Group :
 .. If let `switchLabel : blockStatement` be `switchCase`:
  ... Let <<SwitchLabel_table_ok, `TC tid~table~ b~last~ |- switchLabel : switchLabelIR`>>.
  ... Let `TC~post~`, `f~post~`, and `blockStatementIR` be the result of <<Block_ok, typing `blockStatement`, under typing context `TC` and abstract control flow `f`>>.
  ... Let `switchCaseIR` be `switchLabelIR : blockStatementIR`.
  ... Result in `f~post~`, `switchCaseIR`, and `switchLabel`.
 .. Else let `switchLabel :` be `switchCase`:
  ... Let <<SwitchLabel_table_ok, `TC tid~table~ b~last~ |- switchLabel : switchLabelIR`>>.
  ... Let `switchCaseIR` be `switchLabelIR :`.
  ... Result in `f`, `switchCaseIR`, and `switchLabel`.


relation SwitchCases_table_ok: `TC`, `f`, `tid~table~`, and `switchCase^{asterisk}^`


. If `switchCase^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `f`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `switchCase~h~ :: switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^` be `switchCase^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `b~last~` be `switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`.
  ... Let <<SwitchCase_table_ok, `TC f tid~table~ b~last~ |- switchCase~h~ : f~h~ switchCaseIR~h~ # switchLabel~h~`>>.
  ... Let <<SwitchCases_table_ok, `TC f~h~ tid~table~ |- switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^ : f~t~ switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `f~t~`, `switchCaseIR~h~ :: switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, and `switchLabel~h~ :: switchLabel~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation SwitchLabel_general_ok: `TC`, `typeIR`, `bool`, and `switchLabel`


. Group :
 .. If `bool` is equal to true:
  ... Check that `switchLabel` matches pattern `DEFAULT`.
  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.
 .. Else if let `expressionNonBrace~label~` be `switchLabel`:
  ... Let `expression~label~` be <<expressionNonBrace_as_expression, the expression corresponding to `expressionNonBrace~label~`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~label~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~label~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~label_cast~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~label~`  to  `typeIR`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( _ ctk )` be `typedExpressionIR~label_cast~`.
  ... Check that `ctk` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~label_cast~`.


relation SwitchCase_general_ok: `TC`, `f`, `typeIR~switch~`, `b~last~`, and `switchCase`


. Group :
 .. If let `switchLabel : blockStatement` be `switchCase`:
  ... Let <<SwitchLabel_general_ok, `TC typeIR~switch~ b~last~ |- switchLabel : switchLabelIR`>>.
  ... Let `TC~post~`, `f~post~`, and `blockStatementIR` be the result of <<Block_ok, typing `blockStatement`, under typing context `TC` and abstract control flow `f`>>.
  ... Let `switchCaseIR` be `switchLabelIR : blockStatementIR`.
  ... Result in `f~post~`, `switchCaseIR`, and `switchLabel`.
 .. Else let `switchLabel :` be `switchCase`:
  ... Let <<SwitchLabel_general_ok, `TC typeIR~switch~ b~last~ |- switchLabel : switchLabelIR`>>.
  ... Let `switchCaseIR` be `switchLabelIR :`.
  ... Result in `f`, `switchCaseIR`, and `switchLabel`.


relation SwitchCases_general_ok: `TC`, `f`, `typeIR~switch~`, and `switchCase^{asterisk}^`


. If `switchCase^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `f`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `switchCase~h~ :: switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^` be `switchCase^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `b~last~` be `switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`.
  ... Let <<SwitchCase_general_ok, `TC f typeIR~switch~ b~last~ |- switchCase~h~ : f~h~ switchCaseIR~h~ # switchLabel~h~`>>.
  ... Let <<SwitchCases_general_ok, `TC f~h~ typeIR~switch~ |- switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^ : f~t~ switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `f~t~`, `switchCaseIR~h~ :: switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, and `switchLabel~h~ :: switchLabel~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Decl_object_ok: `p`, `TC~0~`, `typeFrame`, `rdenv`, and `objectDeclaration`


. If let `annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement` be `objectDeclaration`:
 .. Group functionDeclaration:
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `TC~0~`[BLOCK.KIND = `EXTERN`].
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `TC~1~`[BLOCK.FRAME = `typeFrame`].
  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeParameterListOpt, the list of type parameters in `typeParameterListOpt`>>.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be <<name, the name of `typeParameter`>>.
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `<<add_types, $add_types(LOCAL, TC~2~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, TID tid~expl~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~ret~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `typeOrVoid`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~3~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parameterList, the list of parameters in `parameterList`>>.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~3~`>>.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~4~` be `<<add_parameters, $add_parameters(LOCAL, TC~3~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `TC~5~` be `TC~4~`[LOCAL.KIND = `EXTERN_METHOD -> typeIR~ret~`].
  ... Let `_`, `f`, and `blockStatementIR` be the result of <<Block_ok, typing `blockStatement`, under typing context `TC~5~` and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Else if `f` matches pattern `RET`:
   .... Let `rid` be `<<rid, $rid(name, parameterList)>>`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
   .... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `methodTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
   .... If <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `routineTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(p, TC~0~)>>`>>:
    ..... Let `rdenv~init~` be `<<update_map, $update_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)>>`.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
    ..... Let `functionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
    ..... Result in `typeFrame`, `rdenv~init~`, and `functionDeclarationIR`.
  ... Else if `typeIR~ret~` is equal to `VOID`:
   .... Let `rid` be `<<rid, $rid(name, parameterList)>>`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
   .... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `methodTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
   .... If <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `routineTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `<<bound, $bound(p, TC~0~)>>`>>:
    ..... Let `rdenv~init~` be `<<update_map, $update_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)>>`.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
    ..... Let `functionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
    ..... Result in `typeFrame`, `rdenv~init~`, and `functionDeclarationIR`.
. Else let `instantiation` be `objectDeclaration`:
 .. Group instantiation:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `instantiation`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC~0~`,
* and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `instantiationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Let `_ _ _ < _ > ( _ ) nameIR _ ;` be `instantiationIR`.
  ... Let!~option~ `varTypeIR` be `<<find_var, $find_var(p, TC~1~, ` nameIR)>>`.
  ... Let `typeFrame~init~` be `<<update_map, $update_map<id, varTypeIR>(typeFrame, nameIR, varTypeIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `typeFrame~init~`, `rdenv`, and `instantiationIR`.


relation Decls_object_ok: `p`, `TC`, `typeFrame'`, `rdenv'`, and `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^`


. If `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `typeFrame'`, `rdenv'`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `objectDeclaration~h~ :: objectDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^` be `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<Decl_object_ok, `p TC typeFrame' rdenv' |- objectDeclaration~h~ : typeFrame~1~ rdenv~1~ objectDeclarationIR~h~`>>.
  ... Let <<Decls_object_ok, `p TC typeFrame~1~ rdenv~1~ |- objectDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^ : typeFrame~2~ rdenv~2~ objectDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `typeFrame~2~`, `rdenv~2~`, and `objectDeclarationIR~h~ :: objectDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Enum_serializable_field_ok: `TC~0~`, `nameIR~enum~`, `typeIR`, and `name = expression`


. Group :
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
 .. Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR`  to  `typeIR`>>.
 .. Check that `<<ctk_of_expression, $ctk_of_expression(typedExpressionIR~cast~)>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
 .. Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~cast~`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
 .. Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR~enum~` be `ENUM nameIR~enum~ # typeIR { [ ] }`.
 .. Let `value~enum~` be `nameIR~enum~ . nameIR # value`.
 .. Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_var, $add_var(BLOCK, TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~enum~ LCTK ?value~enum~)>>`.
 .. Result in `TC~1~`, `nameIR = typedExpressionIR~cast~`, and `value`.


relation Enum_serializable_fields_ok: `TC'`, `nameIR~enum~`, `typeIR`, and `namedExpression^{asterisk}^`


. If `namedExpression^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `TC'`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `namedExpression~h~ :: namedExpression~t~^{asterisk}^` be `namedExpression^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<Enum_serializable_field_ok, `TC' nameIR~enum~ typeIR |- namedExpression~h~ : TC~1~ namedExpressionIR~h~ # value~field_h~`>>.
  ... Let <<Enum_serializable_fields_ok, `TC~1~ nameIR~enum~ typeIR |- namedExpression~t~^{asterisk}^ : TC~2~ namedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^ # value~field_t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Let `namedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^` be `namedExpressionIR~h~ :: namedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `value~field~^{asterisk}^` be `value~field_h~ :: value~field_t~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Result in `TC~2~`, `namedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`, and `value~field~^{asterisk}^`.


relation SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `TC`, `typeIR~key~`, and `simpleKeysetExpression`


. Let!~type~ `expression` be `simpleKeysetExpression`.
. Group expression-set-alpha:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR''` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Let!~type~ `SET < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''`.
 .. Let!~type~ `[typeIR]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
 .. If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR` and `typeIR~key~` are the same type>>:
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR`.
. Group expression-set-subtype:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR''` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Let!~type~ `SET < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''`.
 .. Let!~type~ `[typeIR]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
 .. If <<Type_alpha, `typeIR` and `typeIR~key~` are not the same type>>:
  ... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>:
   .... Let `typeIR~cast~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be `( typeIR~cast~ ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR~cast~ DYN )`.
   .... Result in `typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. Group expression-non-set:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Check that `~<<is_set_typeIR, $is_set_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
 .. If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>:
  ... Let `typeIR~cast~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be `( typeIR~cast~ ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR~cast~ DYN )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. If let `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group mask:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_mask)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~ &&& typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~`.
. Else if let `expression~l~ .. expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group range:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_range)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Check that `typeIR~reduced~` is equal to <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~ .. typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~`.
. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `DEFAULT`:
 .. Group default:
  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.
. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare:
  ... Result in `_`.


relation SelectCase_keyset_ok: `TC`, `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`, and `keysetExpression`


. Let!~type~ `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
. If let `expression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-expression:
  ... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
. Else if let `tupleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. If let `( expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-mask:
   .... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
 .. Else if let `( expression~l~ .. expression~r~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-range:
   .... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ .. expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
. Let!~type~ `simpleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`.
. If let `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-mask:
  ... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
. Else if let `expression~l~ .. expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-range:
  ... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ .. expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
. If let `simpleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. If `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `DEFAULT`:
  ... Group simpleKeysetExpression-default:
   .... If `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`:
    ..... Result in `DEFAULT`.
   .... Let `typeIR''^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Else if let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR''^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
   .... Else if the length of `typeIR''^{asterisk}^` is greater than 1:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR''^{asterisk}^ > |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
 .. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `_`:
  ... Group simpleKeysetExpression-dontcare:
   .... Let `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Else if let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
   .... Else if the length of `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is greater than 1:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ > |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
. Else let `tupleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. If `tupleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `( DEFAULT )`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-default:
   .... Let `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Else if let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
   .... Else if the length of `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is greater than 1:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ > |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
 .. Else if `tupleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `( _ )`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-dontcare:
   .... Let `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Else if let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
   .... Else if the length of `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is greater than 1:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ > |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
 .. Else if let `( simpleKeysetExpression~h~ , simpleKeysetExpressionList~t~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-list:
   .... Let `simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_simpleKeysetExpressionList, the list of simple keyset expressions in `simpleKeysetExpressionList~t~`>>.
   .... Let `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^` be `simpleKeysetExpression~h~ :: simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that the length of `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `simpleKeysetExpressionIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR''' |- simpleKeysetExpression : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
--
+
for each `simpleKeysetExpression` in `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR'''` in `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`
   .... Result in `( simpleKeysetExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ )`.


relation SelectCase_ok: `TC`, `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`, `typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^`, and `keysetExpression : name ;`


. Group :
 .. Let <<SelectCase_keyset_ok, `TC typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^ |- keysetExpression : keysetExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
 .. Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Result in `keysetExpressionIR : nameIR ;`.


relation TableEntry_keyset_simple_ok: `TC`, `TBLC`, (`typeIR~key~`, `text`), and `simpleKeysetExpression`


. If let `expression` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group expression:
  ... If `text` is equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Let `matchMode` be `TBLC.MODE`.
   .... Let!~type~ `NOPRILPM n` be `matchMode`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Let `ctk` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>:
    ..... Let `typeIR~set~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
    ..... Let `typedExpressionIR~set~` be `( typeIR~set~ ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR~set~ ctk )`.
    ..... Result in `LPM n` and `typedExpressionIR~set~`.
  ... Else `text` is not equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Let `ctk` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>:
    ..... Let `typeIR~set~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
    ..... Let `typedExpressionIR~set~` be `( typeIR~set~ ) typedExpressionIR # ( typeIR~set~ ctk )`.
    ..... Result in `NOLPM` and `typedExpressionIR~set~`.
. If let `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group mask:
  ... If `text` is equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Let `matchMode` be `TBLC.MODE`.
   .... Let!~type~ `NOPRILPM n` be `matchMode`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_mask)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
   .... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~reduced~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>:
    ..... Check that `ctk~r_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
    ..... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Let `i~r~` be `<<to_number, $to_number(value~r~)>>`.
    ..... Let `n~prefix~` be `<<tableEntry_lpm_prefix, $tableEntry_lpm_prefix(n W <<to_bitstr, $to_bitstr(n, i~r~)>>)>>`.
    ..... Result in `LPM n~prefix~` and `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ &&& typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`.
  ... Else if `text` is equal to `"ternary"`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
   .... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_mask)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
   .... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~reduced~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>:
    ..... Result in `NOLPM` and `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ &&& typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`.
. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `DEFAULT`:
 .. Group default:
  ... If `text` is equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Let `matchMode` be `TBLC.MODE`.
   .... Let!~type~ `NOPRILPM n` be `matchMode`.
   .... Result in `LPM n` and `DEFAULT`.
  ... Else `text` is not equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Check that `text` is not equal to `"exact"`.
   .... Result in `NOLPM` and `DEFAULT`.
. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare:
  ... If `text` is equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Let `matchMode` be `TBLC.MODE`.
   .... Let!~type~ `NOPRILPM _` be `matchMode`.
   .... Result in `LPM 0` and `_`.
  ... Else `text` is not equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Check that `text` is not equal to `"exact"`.
   .... Result in `NOLPM` and `_`.
. Else if `text` is equal to `"range"`:
 .. Let!~type~ `expression~l~ .. expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`.
 .. Group range-range:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Let!~option~ `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_range)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... If <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~reduced~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>:
   .... Result in `NOLPM` and `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ .. typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`.


relation TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok: `TC`, `TBLC`, `TBLS'`, `matchKey^{asterisk}^`, and `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^`


. If `matchKey^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Check that `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `TBLS'` and `[ ]`.
. Else let `matchKey~h~ :: matchKey~t~^{asterisk}^` be `matchKey^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Let!~type~ `simpleKeysetExpression~h~ :: simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^` be `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<TableEntry_keyset_simple_ok, `TC TBLC |- matchKey~h~ @ simpleKeysetExpression~h~ : TBLS~1~ simpleKeysetExpressionIR~h~`>>.
  ... Let `TBLS~2~` be `<<join_tableEntryState, $join_tableEntryState(TBLS', TBLS~1~)>>`.
  ... Let <<TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok, `TC TBLC TBLS~2~ |- matchKey~t~^{asterisk}^ @ simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^ : TBLS~3~ simpleKeysetExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `TBLS~3~` and `simpleKeysetExpressionIR~h~ :: simpleKeysetExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Expr_lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `expressionIR # ( _ _ )`


. If let `prefixedNameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR:
  ... Let!~option~ `direction _ ctk _^?^` be `<<find_var, $find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `ctk` matches pattern `DYN`.
  ... If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `memberAccessBaseIR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Let!~type~ `typedExpressionIR~base~` be `memberAccessBaseIR`.
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-memberAccessExpressionIR:
  ... If <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>>:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Else if let `typeIR [ _ ]` be `typeIR'`:
    ..... If `nameIR` is equal to `"next"`:
     ...... If `p = BLOCK /\ <<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
      ....... The relation holds.
     ...... Else if `p = LOCAL /\ <<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
      ....... The relation holds.
    ..... Else if `nameIR` is equal to `"last"`:
     ...... If `p = BLOCK /\ <<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
      ....... The relation holds.
     ...... Else if `p = LOCAL /\ <<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
      ....... The relation holds.
   .... Else if `~<<is_headerStackTypeIR, $is_headerStackTypeIR(<<canon, $canon(typeIR~base~)>>)>>`:
    ..... The relation holds.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index~ ]` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-indexAccessExpressionIR:
  ... If <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>>:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ]` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-indexAccessExpressionIR-bitslice:
  ... If <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>>:
   .... The relation holds.


relation Expr_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `expressionIR # _`


. If let `booleanLiteral` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-boolean:
  ... If `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `TRUE`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `B true`.
  ... Else `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `FALSE`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `B false`.
. Else if let `numberLiteral` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-number:
  ... If let `D i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `D i`.
  ... Else if let `n W i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `n W i`.
  ... Else let `n S i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `n S i`.
. Else if let `" text "` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-stringLiteral:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `" text "`.
. Else if let `prefixedNameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value` be `<<find_value_inst, $find_value_inst(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `STO'` and `value`.
. Else if let `defaultExpression` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group defaultExpressionIR:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `DEFAULT`.
. Else if let `unop typedExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group unaryExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and <<un_op, `unop` `value`>>.
. Let `( _ _ )` be `_`.
. If let `typedExpressionIR~l~ binop' typedExpressionIR~r~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group binaryExpressionIR:
  ... Check that `~binop' is in [&&, ||]`.
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~l~ ==> STO~1~ value~l~`>>.
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~r~ ==> STO~2~ value~r~`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~2~` and <<bin_op, `value~l~` `binop'` `value~r~`>>.
  ... If `binop'` matches pattern `&&`:
   .... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~l~ ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Result in `STO~1~` and `B false`.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~r~ ==> STO~2~ value~r~`>>.
    ..... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~r~`.
  ... Else if `binop'` matches pattern `||`:
   .... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~l~ ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Result in `STO~1~` and `B true`.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~r~ ==> STO~2~ value~r~`>>.
    ..... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~r~`.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~cond~ ? typedExpressionIR~true~ : typedExpressionIR~false~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group ternaryExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~cond~ ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
   .... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~true~ ==> STO~2~ value~true~`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~true~`.
  ... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
   .... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~false~ ==> STO~2~ value~false~`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~false~`.
. Else if let `( typeIR ) typedExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group castExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Let `value~cast~` be `<<cast_op, $cast_op(typeIR, value)>>`.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `value~cast~`.
. Else if let `dataExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Check that `dataExpressionIR` matches pattern `{#}`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-invalid:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `{#}`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-sequence:
  ... If let `SEQ { typedExpressionListIR }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionListIR ==> STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `SEQ ( value^{asterisk}^ )`.
  ... Else if let `SEQ { typedExpressionListIR , ... }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionListIR ==> STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `SEQ ( value^{asterisk}^ , ... )`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-record:
  ... If let `RECORD { nameIR = typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ ==> STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `RECORD { value nameIR ;^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Else if let `RECORD { nameIR = typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ ==> STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `RECORD { value nameIR ;^{asterisk}^ , ... }`.
. Else if let `ERROR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group errorAccessExpressionIR:
  ... Let `nameIR~error~` be `"error." ++ nameIR`.
  ... Let `value~error~` be `<<find_value_inst, $find_value_inst(p, IC, ` nameIR~error~)>>`.
  ... Result in `STO'` and `value~error~`.
. Else if let `memberAccessBaseIR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Else if let `TYPE prefixedNameIR` be `memberAccessBaseIR`:
  ... Group memberAccessExpressionIR-type:
   .... Let!~option~ `typeDefIR` be `<<find_typedef_inst, $find_typedef_inst(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
   .... Let!~type~ `enumTypeIR` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... If let `ENUM tid { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Result in `STO'` and `tid . nameIR`.
   .... Else let `ENUM tid # _ { id~member~ = value~member~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Let!~option~ `value` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, value>(nameIR, (id~member~, value~member~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
    ..... Result in `STO'` and `tid . nameIR # value`.
 .. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be `memberAccessBaseIR`:
  ... Check that `nameIR` is equal to `"size"`.
  ... Group memberAccessExpressionIR-expression-stack-size:
   .... Let `_ # ( typeIR _ )` be `typedExpressionIR~base~`.
   .... Check that `typeIR` is equal to `_`.
   .... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `_`>>.
   .... Let!~type~ `_ [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
   .... Result in `STO'` and `D n~size~`.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ]` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group sliceAccessExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~base~ ==> STO~1~ value~base~`>>.
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~hi~ ==> STO~2~ value~hi~`>>.
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~2~ |- typedExpressionIR~lo~ ==> STO~3~ value~lo~`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~3~` and `<<bitacc_op, $bitacc_op(value~base~, value~hi~, value~lo~)>>`.
. Else if let `callExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. If let `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR )` be `callExpressionIR`:
  ... Group callExpressionIR-constructor:
   .... Let!~option~ `(_, constructor, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<find_constructor_inst, $find_constructor_inst(IC, prefixedNameIR, argumentListIR)>>`.
   .... Let <<Constructor_inst, `p IC STO' |- constructor < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) ==> STO~1~ object`>>.
   .... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, IC.PATH, object)>>`.
   .... Let `value~ref~` be `! IC.PATH`.
   .... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~ref~`.
 .. Else let `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callExpressionIR`:
  ... Else if `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
   .... Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... Group callExpressionIR-builtin-size:
    ..... If let `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR` be `routineTargetIR`:
     ...... Let `_ # ( _ _ )` be `typedExpressionIR~base~`.
     ...... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
     ...... Result in `STO'` and `<<sizeof, $sizeof(_, nameIR)>>`.
    ..... Else if let `TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR` be `routineTargetIR`:
     ...... Let!~option~ `typeDefIR` be `<<find_typedef_inst, $find_typedef_inst(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
     ...... If let `_` be `typeDefIR`:
      ....... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
      ....... Result in `STO'` and `<<sizeof, $sizeof(_, nameIR)>>`.
     ...... Else let `_ < tid^{asterisk}^ , tid'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeDefIR`:
      ....... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
      ....... Check that `tid'^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
      ....... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
      ....... Result in `STO'` and `<<sizeof, $sizeof(_, nameIR)>>`.
  ... Let `routineTargetIR' < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR )` be `callExpressionIR`.
  ... Else if let `( routineTargetIR )` be `routineTargetIR'`:
   .... Group callExpressionIR-parenthesized:
    ..... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- routineTargetIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) # _ ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
    ..... Result in `STO~1~` and `value`.
. Else if let `( typedExpressionIR )` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group parenthesizedExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `value`.


relation Exprs_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `[ ]`.
. Else let `typedExpressionIR~h~ :: typedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~h~ ==> STO~1~ value~h~`>>.
  ... Let <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> STO~2~ value~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~h~ :: value~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Argument_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, and `argumentIR`


. If let `typedExpressionIR` be `argumentIR`:
 .. Group typedExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~0~ |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `value`.
. Else if let `nameIR = typedExpressionIR` be `argumentIR`:
 .. Group nameIR-typedExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~0~ |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `value`.


relation Stmt_inst: `p'`, `IC'`, `STO'`, and `statementIR`


. If let `emptyStatementIR` be `statementIR`:
 .. Group emptyStatementIR:
  ... Result in 
* the instantiation context `IC'`,
* the updated store `STO'`,
* and the instantiated statement `emptyStatementIR`.
. Else if let `assignmentStatementIR` be `statementIR`:
 .. Group assignmentStatementIR:
  ... Result in 
* the instantiation context `IC'`,
* the updated store `STO'`,
* and the instantiated statement `assignmentStatementIR`.
. Else if let `callStatementIR` be `statementIR`:
 .. Group callStatementIR:
  ... Result in 
* the instantiation context `IC'`,
* the updated store `STO'`,
* and the instantiated statement `callStatementIR`.
. Else if let `prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentListIR ) ;` be `statementIR`:
 .. Group directApplicationStatementIR:
  ... Let!~option~ `(_, constructor, _^{asterisk}^)` be `<<find_constructor_inst, $find_constructor_inst(IC', prefixedNameIR, [ ])>>`.
  ... Let <<Constructor_inst, `p' IC' STO' |- constructor < [ ] > ( [ ] # [ ] ) ==> STO~1~ object`>>.
  ... Let `tid~fresh~` be <<fresh_tid, a fresh type variable>>.
  ... Let `tid` be <<flatten_prefixedNameIR, the string form of  `prefixedNameIR`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR` be `TID tid`.
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<concat_text, the concatenation of `[tid, "_", tid~fresh~]`>>.
  ... Let `oid` be `IC'.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
  ... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object)>>`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
  ... Let `routineTargetIR` be `` tid # ( typeIR CTK ) . "apply"`.
  ... Let `callStatementIR` be `routineTargetIR < [ ] > ( argumentListIR ) ;`.
  ... Let `blockStatementIR` be `{ [constantDeclarationIR, callStatementIR] }`.
  ... Result in 
* the instantiation context `IC'`,
* the updated store `STO~2~`,
* and the instantiated statement `blockStatementIR`.
. Else if let `exitStatementIR` be `statementIR`:
 .. Group exitStatementIR:
  ... Result in 
* the instantiation context `IC'`,
* the updated store `STO'`,
* and the instantiated statement `exitStatementIR`.
. Else if let `conditionalStatementIR` be `statementIR`:
 .. Group conditionalStatementIR:
  ... If let `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~` be `conditionalStatementIR`:
   .... Let `IC~then~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR~then_inst~` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `statementIR~then~`, under cursor `p'`, instantiation context `IC'`, and store `STO'`>>.
   .... Result in 
* the instantiation context `IC'`,
* the updated store `STO~1~`,
* and the instantiated statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then_inst~`.
  ... Else let `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~ ELSE statementIR~else~` be `conditionalStatementIR`:
   .... Let `IC~then~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR~then_inst~` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `statementIR~then~`, under cursor `p'`, instantiation context `IC'`, and store `STO'`>>.
   .... Let `IC~else~`, `STO~2~`, and `statementIR~else_inst~` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `statementIR~else~`, under cursor `p'`, instantiation context `IC'`, and store `STO~1~`>>.
   .... Result in 
* the instantiation context `IC'`,
* the updated store `STO~2~`,
* and the instantiated statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then_inst~ ELSE statementIR~else_inst~`.
. Else if let `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR ) { switchCaseListIR }` be `statementIR`:
 .. Group switchStatementIR:
  ... Let <<SwitchCases_inst, `p' IC' STO' |- switchCaseListIR ==> STO~1~ switchCaseListIR~inst~`>>.
  ... Result in 
* the instantiation context `IC'`,
* the updated store `STO~1~`,
* and the instantiated statement `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR ) { switchCaseListIR~inst~ }`.
. Check that `p'` matches pattern `LOCAL`.
. If let `returnStatementIR` be `statementIR`:
 .. Group returnStatementIR:
  ... Result in 
* the instantiation context `IC'`,
* the updated store `STO'`,
* and the instantiated statement `returnStatementIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR }` be `statementIR`:
 .. Group blockStatementIR:
  ... Let <<Block_inst, `IC' STO' |- annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR } ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ _ { blockElementStatementListIR~inst~ }`>>.
  ... Result in 
* the instantiation context `IC~1~`,
* the updated store `STO~1~`,
* and the instantiated statement `annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR~inst~ }`.


relation BlockElementStmt_inst: `IC~0'~`, `STO~0'~`, and `blockElementStatementIR`


. If let `constantDeclarationIR` be `blockElementStatementIR`:
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `LOCAL IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- constantDeclarationIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `?declarationIR` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Let!~type~ `constantDeclarationIR~inst~` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and ?`constantDeclarationIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `variableDeclarationIR` be `blockElementStatementIR`:
 .. Group variableDeclarationIR:
  ... Result in `IC~0'~`, `STO~0'~`, and ?`variableDeclarationIR`.
. Else let `statementIR` be `blockElementStatementIR`:
 .. Group statementIR:
  ... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR~inst~` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `statementIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, instantiation context `IC~0'~`, and store `STO~0'~`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and ?`statementIR~inst~`.


relation BlockElementStmts_inst: `IC'`, `STO'`, and `blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `IC'`, `STO'`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `blockElementStatementIR~h~ :: blockElementStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<BlockElementStmt_inst, `IC' STO' |- blockElementStatementIR~h~ ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ blockElementStatementIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `?blockElementStatementIR~h_inst~` be `blockElementStatementIR'^?^`.
  ... Let <<BlockElementStmts_inst, `IC~1~ STO~1~ |- blockElementStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~2~ STO~2~ blockElementStatementIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `blockElementStatementIR~h_inst~ :: blockElementStatementIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Block_inst: `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR }`


. Group :
 .. Let `IC~1~` be `<<enter_inst, $enter_inst(IC~0~)>>`.
 .. Let <<BlockElementStmts_inst, `IC~1~ STO~0~ |- blockElementStatementListIR ==> IC~2~ STO~1~ blockElementStatementListIR~inst~`>>.
 .. Let `IC~3~` be `<<exit_inst, $exit_inst(IC~2~)>>`.
 .. Result in `IC~3~`, `STO~1~`, and `annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR~inst~ }`.


relation ExternMethod_inst: `IC~0~` and `externMethodPrototypeIR`


. If let `annotationList typeIR nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) ;` be `externMethodPrototypeIR`:
 .. Group non-abstract:
  ... Let `rid` be `<<rid_IR, $rid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `method` be `EXTERN_METHOD < typeParameterListIR ++ typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) ?{ [ ] }`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_routine_overload_inst, $add_routine_overload_inst(BLOCK, IC~0~, rid, method)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`.
. Else let `annotationList ABSTRACT typeIR nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) ;` be `externMethodPrototypeIR`:
 .. Group abstract:
  ... Let `rid` be `<<rid_IR, $rid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `method` be `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT < typeParameterListIR ++ typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR )`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_routine_overload_inst, $add_routine_overload_inst(BLOCK, IC~0~, rid, method)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`.


relation ExternMethods_inst: `IC'` and `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `IC'`.
. Else let `externMethodPrototypeIR~h~ :: externMethodPrototypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<ExternMethod_inst, `IC' |- externMethodPrototypeIR~h~ ==> IC~1~`>>.
  ... Let <<ExternMethods_inst, `IC~1~ |- externMethodPrototypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~2~`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`.


relation ParserStmt_inst: `IC~0'~`, `STO~0~`, and `parserStatementIR`


. If let `constantDeclarationIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `LOCAL IC~0'~ STO~0~ |- constantDeclarationIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `?declarationIR` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Let!~type~ `constantDeclarationIR~inst~` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `constantDeclarationIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `variableDeclarationIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group variableDeclarationIR:
  ... Let <<BlockElementStmt_inst, `IC~0'~ STO~0~ |- variableDeclarationIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ blockElementStatementIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `?blockElementStatementIR` be `blockElementStatementIR'^?^`.
  ... Let!~type~ `variableDeclarationIR~inst~` be `blockElementStatementIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `variableDeclarationIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `emptyStatementIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group emptyStatementIR:
  ... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `emptyStatementIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, instantiation context `IC~0'~`, and store `STO~0~`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `emptyStatementIR~inst~` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `emptyStatementIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `assignmentStatementIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group assignmentStatementIR:
  ... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `assignmentStatementIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, instantiation context `IC~0'~`, and store `STO~0~`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `assignmentStatementIR~inst~` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `assignmentStatementIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `callStatementIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group callStatementIR:
  ... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `callStatementIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, instantiation context `IC~0'~`, and store `STO~0~`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `callStatementIR~inst~` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `callStatementIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentListIR ) ;` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group directApplicationStatementIR:
  ... Let!~option~ `(_, constructor, _^{asterisk}^)` be `<<find_constructor_inst, $find_constructor_inst(IC~0'~, prefixedNameIR, [ ])>>`.
  ... Let <<Constructor_inst, `LOCAL IC~0'~ STO~0~ |- constructor < [ ] > ( [ ] # [ ] ) ==> STO~1~ object`>>.
  ... Let `tid` be <<flatten_prefixedNameIR, the string form of  `prefixedNameIR`>>.
  ... Let `tid~fresh~` be <<fresh_tid, a fresh type variable>>.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `tid ++ "_" ++ tid~fresh~`.
  ... Let `oid` be `IC~0'~.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
  ... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR` be `TID tid`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
  ... Let `routineTargetIR` be `` tid # ( typeIR CTK ) . "apply"`.
  ... Let `callStatementIR` be `routineTargetIR < [ ] > ( argumentListIR ) ;`.
  ... Let `parserBlockStatementIR` be `{ [constantDeclarationIR, callStatementIR] }`.
  ... Result in `IC~0'~`, `STO~2~`, and `parserBlockStatementIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList { parserStatementListIR }` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group parserBlockStatementIR:
  ... Let <<ParserStmts_inst, `IC~0'~ STO~0~ |- parserStatementListIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ parserStatementListIR~inst~`>>.
  ... Let `parserBlockStatementIR~inst~` be `annotationList { parserStatementListIR~inst~ }`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `parserBlockStatementIR~inst~`.
. Else let `conditionalStatementIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group conditionalStatementIR:
  ... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `conditionalStatementIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, instantiation context `IC~0'~`, and store `STO~0~`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `conditionalStatementIR~inst~` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `conditionalStatementIR~inst~`.


relation ParserStmts_inst: `IC'`, `STO'`, and `parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `IC'`, `STO'`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `parserStatementIR~h~ :: parserStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<ParserStmt_inst, `IC' STO' |- parserStatementIR~h~ ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ parserStatementIR~h_inst~`>>.
  ... Let <<ParserStmts_inst, `IC~1~ STO~1~ |- parserStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~2~ STO~2~ parserStatementIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `parserStatementIR~h_inst~ :: parserStatementIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ParserState_inst: `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `annotationList STATE nameIR { parserStatementListIR transitionStatementIR }`


. Group :
 .. Let <<ParserStmts_inst, `IC~0~ STO~0~ |- parserStatementListIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ parserStatementListIR~inst~`>>.
 .. Let `state` be `annotationList { parserStatementListIR~inst~ transitionStatementIR }`.
 .. Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_state_inst, $add_state_inst(BLOCK, IC~1~, nameIR, state)>>`.
 .. Result in `IC~2~` and `STO~1~`.


relation ParserStates_inst: `IC'`, `STO'`, and `parserStateIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `parserStateIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `IC'` and `STO'`.
. Else let `parserStateIR~h~ :: parserStateIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parserStateIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<ParserState_inst, `IC' STO' |- parserStateIR~h~ ==> IC~1~ STO~1~`>>.
  ... Let <<ParserStates_inst, `IC~1~ STO~1~ |- parserStateIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~2~ STO~2~`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~2~` and `STO~2~`.


relation ParserLocalDecl_inst: `IC~0'~`, `STO~0'~`, and `parserLocalDeclarationIR`


. If let `constantDeclarationIR` be `parserLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `BLOCK IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- constantDeclarationIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `?declarationIR` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Let!~type~ `constantDeclarationIR~inst~` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `constantDeclarationIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `instantiationIR` be `parserLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group instantiationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `BLOCK IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- instantiationIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `?declarationIR` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Let!~type~ `constantDeclarationIR~inst~` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `constantDeclarationIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `variableDeclarationIR` be `parserLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group variableDeclarationIR:
  ... Result in `IC~0'~`, `STO~0'~`, and `variableDeclarationIR`.
. Else let `valueSetDeclarationIR` be `parserLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group valueSetDeclarationIR:
  ... Result in `IC~0'~`, `STO~0'~`, and `valueSetDeclarationIR`.


relation ParserLocalDecls_inst: `IC'`, `STO'`, and `parserLocalDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `parserLocalDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `IC'`, `STO'`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `parserLocalDeclarationIR~h~ :: parserLocalDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parserLocalDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<ParserLocalDecl_inst, `IC' STO' |- parserLocalDeclarationIR~h~ ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ parserLocalDeclarationIR~h_inst~`>>.
  ... Let <<ParserLocalDecls_inst, `IC~1~ STO~1~ |- parserLocalDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~2~ STO~2~ parserLocalDeclarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `parserLocalDeclarationIR~h_inst~ :: parserLocalDeclarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.


relation TableProperty_inst: `IC`, `STO'`, and `tablePropertyIR`


. If let `KEY = { tableKeyListIR }` be `tablePropertyIR`:
 .. Group key:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `KEY = { tableKeyListIR }`.
. Else if let `ACTIONS = { tableActionListIR }` be `tablePropertyIR`:
 .. Group actions:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `ACTIONS = { tableActionListIR }`.
. Else if let `annotationList constOptIR ENTRIES = { tableEntryListIR }` be `tablePropertyIR`:
 .. Group entries:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `annotationList constOptIR ENTRIES = { tableEntryListIR }`.
. Else if let `annotationList constOptIR DEFAULT_ACTION = tableActionReferenceIR ;` be `tablePropertyIR`:
 .. Group custom-default-action:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `annotationList constOptIR DEFAULT_ACTION = tableActionReferenceIR ;`.
. Else if let `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM nameIR = typedExpressionIR ;` be `tablePropertyIR`:
 .. Group custom:
  ... Let `IC~inner~` be `<<enter_path, $enter_path(IC, nameIR)>>`.
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `LOCAL IC~inner~ STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST nameIR = value ;`.
. Else let `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST nameIR constantInitializerIR ;` be `tablePropertyIR`:
 .. Group custom-const:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST nameIR constantInitializerIR ;`.


relation TableProperties_inst: `IC`, `STO'`, and `tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `[ ]`.
. Else let `tablePropertyIR~h~ :: tablePropertyIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<TableProperty_inst, `IC STO' |- tablePropertyIR~h~ ==> STO~1~ tablePropertyIR~h_inst~`>>.
  ... Let <<TableProperties_inst, `IC STO~1~ |- tablePropertyIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> STO~2~ tablePropertyIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~2~` and `tablePropertyIR~h_inst~ :: tablePropertyIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ControlLocalDecl_inst: `IC~0'~`, `STO~0'~`, and `controlLocalDeclarationIR`


. If let `constantDeclarationIR` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `BLOCK IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- constantDeclarationIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `?declarationIR` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Let!~type~ `constantDeclarationIR~inst~` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and ?`constantDeclarationIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `instantiationIR` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group instantiationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `BLOCK IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- instantiationIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `?declarationIR` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Let!~type~ `constantDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and ?`constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `variableDeclarationIR` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group variableDeclarationIR:
  ... Result in `IC~0'~`, `STO~0'~`, and ?`variableDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `actionDeclarationIR` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group actionDeclarationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `BLOCK IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- actionDeclarationIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR^?^` is None.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and ?().
. Else let `annotationList TABLE typeIR nameIR { tablePropertyListIR }` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group tableDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `IC~inner~` be `<<enter_path, $enter_path(IC~0'~, nameIR)>>`.
  ... Let <<Constructor_inst, `BLOCK IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- TABLE nameIR { tablePropertyListIR } < [ ] > ( [ ] # [ ] ) ==> STO~1~ object~table~`>>.
  ... Let `oid` be `IC~0'~.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
  ... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object~table~)>>`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_value_inst, $add_value_inst(BLOCK, IC~0'~, nameIR, ! oid)>>`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and ?`constantDeclarationIR`.


relation ControlLocalDecls_inst: `IC'`, `STO'`, and `controlLocalDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `controlLocalDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `IC'`, `STO'`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `controlLocalDeclarationIR~h~ :: controlLocalDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons-none:
  ... Let <<ControlLocalDecl_inst, `IC' STO' |- controlLocalDeclarationIR~h~ ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ controlLocalDeclarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `controlLocalDeclarationIR'^?^` is None.
  ... Let <<ControlLocalDecls_inst, `IC~1~ STO~1~ |- controlLocalDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~2~ STO~2~ controlLocalDeclarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `controlLocalDeclarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons-some:
  ... Let <<ControlLocalDecl_inst, `IC' STO' |- controlLocalDeclarationIR~h~ ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ controlLocalDeclarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `?controlLocalDeclarationIR~h_inst~` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Let <<ControlLocalDecls_inst, `IC~1~ STO~1~ |- controlLocalDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~2~ STO~2~ controlLocalDeclarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `controlLocalDeclarationIR~h_inst~ :: controlLocalDeclarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Decl_inst: `cursor'`, `IC~0~`, `STO'`, and `declarationIR`


. If let `annotationList CONST typeIR nameIR = value ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR:
  ... If `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_value_inst, $add_value_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, value)>>`.
   .... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
  ... Else `cursor'` does not match pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_value_inst, $add_value_inst(cursor', IC~0~, nameIR, value)>>`.
   .... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `annotationList CONST typeIR nameIR = value ;`.
   .... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?`constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList typeIR prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) nameIR objectInitializerOptIR ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group instantiationIR:
  ... If `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let!~option~ `(_, constructor, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<find_constructor_inst, $find_constructor_inst(IC~0~, prefixedNameIR, argumentListIR)>>`.
   .... Let `IC~inner~` be `<<enter_path, $enter_path(IC~0~, nameIR)>>`.
   .... Let <<Constructor_inst, `GLOBAL IC~inner~ STO' |- constructor < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) ==> STO~1~ object`>>.
   .... Else if let `EXTERN tid { tenv frame renv }` be `object`:
    ..... Let `IC~decl~` be `<<empty_instantiationContext, $empty_instantiationContext>>`[PATH = `IC~0~.PATH`][GLOBAL = `IC~0~.GLOBAL`].
    ..... Let `objectDeclarationListIR` be `<<flatten_objectInitializerOptIR, $flatten_objectInitializerOptIR(objectInitializerOptIR)>>`.
    ..... Let <<Decls_inst, `BLOCK IC~decl~ STO~1~ |- objectDeclarationListIR ==> IC~decl_post~ STO~2~ _^{asterisk}^`>>.
    ..... Let `frame~merged~` be `<<merge_frames, $merge_frames(frame, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.FRAME)>>`.
    ..... Let `renv~merged~` be `<<merge_renv_with_extern, $merge_renv_with_extern(renv, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.ROUTINE)>>`.
    ..... Let `object~merged~` be `EXTERN tid { tenv frame~merged~ renv~merged~ }`.
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~3~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~2~, oid, object~merged~)>>`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_value_inst, $add_value_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)>>`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~2~`, and ?().
   .... Else if `~<<is_extern_object, $is_extern_object(object)>>`:
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object)>>`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_value_inst, $add_value_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)>>`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and ?().
  ... Else `cursor'` does not match pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let!~option~ `(_, constructor, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<find_constructor_inst, $find_constructor_inst(IC~0~, prefixedNameIR, argumentListIR)>>`.
   .... Let `IC~inner~` be `<<enter_path, $enter_path(IC~0~, nameIR)>>`.
   .... Let <<Constructor_inst, `cursor' IC~inner~ STO' |- constructor < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) ==> STO~1~ object`>>.
   .... Else if let `EXTERN tid { tenv frame renv }` be `object`:
    ..... Let `IC~decl~` be `<<empty_instantiationContext, $empty_instantiationContext>>`[PATH = `IC~0~.PATH`][GLOBAL = `IC~0~.GLOBAL`].
    ..... Let `objectDeclarationListIR` be `<<flatten_objectInitializerOptIR, $flatten_objectInitializerOptIR(objectInitializerOptIR)>>`.
    ..... Let <<Decls_inst, `BLOCK IC~decl~ STO~1~ |- objectDeclarationListIR ==> IC~decl_post~ STO~2~ _^{asterisk}^`>>.
    ..... Let `frame~merged~` be `<<merge_frames, $merge_frames(frame, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.FRAME)>>`.
    ..... Let `renv~merged~` be `<<merge_renv_with_extern, $merge_renv_with_extern(renv, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.ROUTINE)>>`.
    ..... Let `object~merged~` be `EXTERN tid { tenv frame~merged~ renv~merged~ }`.
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~3~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~2~, oid, object~merged~)>>`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_value_inst, $add_value_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)>>`.
    ..... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~2~`, and ?`constantDeclarationIR`.
   .... Else if `~<<is_extern_object, $is_extern_object(object)>>`:
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object)>>`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_value_inst, $add_value_inst(cursor', IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)>>`.
    ..... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and ?`constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList typeIR nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group functionDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `rid` be `<<rid_IR, $rid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `function` be `FUNCTION < typeParameterListIR ++ typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_routine_overload_inst, $add_routine_overload_inst(cursor', IC~0~, rid, function)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList ACTION nameIR ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group actionDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `rid` be `<<rid_IR, $rid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `action` be `ACTION ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_routine_non_overload_inst, $add_routine_non_overload_inst(cursor', IC~0~, rid, action)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Check that `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`.
. If let `ERROR { nameIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group errorDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `nameIR~error~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~error~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `nameIR~error~` be <<concat_text, the concatenation of `["error.", nameIR]`>>.
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `value~error~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~error~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `value~error~` be `ERROR . nameIR`.
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_values_inst, $add_values_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR~error~^{asterisk}^, value~error~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `MATCH_KIND { nameIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group matchKindDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `value~match_kind~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~match_kind~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `value~match_kind~` be `MATCH_KIND . nameIR`.
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_values_inst, $add_values_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR^{asterisk}^, value~match_kind~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList EXTERN typeIR nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group externFunctionDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `rid` be `<<rid_IR, $rid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `function` be `EXTERN_FUNCTION < typeParameterListIR ++ typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR )`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_routine_overload_inst, $add_routine_overload_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, rid, function)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList EXTERN nameIR < typeParameterListIR , > { externConstructorPrototypeIR'^{asterisk}^ externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group externObjectDeclarationIR:
  ... Check that `externConstructorPrototypeIR'^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`.
  ... Let `rid^{asterisk}^` be the list of `rid`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `rid` be <<rid_of_externMethodPrototypeIR, the routine id of  `externMethodPrototypeIR`>>.
--
+
for each `externMethodPrototypeIR` in `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `routineTypeDefIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `routineTypeDefIR` be <<type_of_externMethodPrototypeIR, the routine type definition of  `externMethodPrototypeIR`>>.
--
+
for each `externMethodPrototypeIR` in `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `rdenv` be `{ rid : routineTypeDefIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `externObjectTypeIR` be `EXTERN nameIR rdenv`.
  ... Let `polyTypeDefIR` be `externObjectTypeIR < typeParameterListIR , [ ] >`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, polyTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid_IR, $cid_IR(nameIR, [ ])>>`.
  ... Let `constructor` be `EXTERN nameIR < typeParameterListIR > ( [ ] ) { externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_constructor_inst, $add_constructor_inst(IC~1~, cid, constructor)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO'`, and ?().
  ... Let `externConstructorPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^` be `externConstructorPrototypeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `rid^{asterisk}^` be the list of `rid`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `rid` be <<rid_of_externMethodPrototypeIR, the routine id of  `externMethodPrototypeIR`>>.
--
+
for each `externMethodPrototypeIR` in `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `routineTypeDefIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `routineTypeDefIR` be <<type_of_externMethodPrototypeIR, the routine type definition of  `externMethodPrototypeIR`>>.
--
+
for each `externMethodPrototypeIR` in `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `rdenv` be `{ rid : routineTypeDefIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `externObjectTypeIR` be `EXTERN nameIR rdenv`.
  ... Let `polyTypeDefIR` be `externObjectTypeIR < typeParameterListIR , [ ] >`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, polyTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Let `cid^{asterisk}^` be the list of `cid`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `cid` be <<cid_of_externConstructorPrototypeIR, the constructor id of  `externConstructorPrototypeIR`>>.
--
+
for each `externConstructorPrototypeIR` in `externConstructorPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `constructor^{asterisk}^` be the list of `constructor`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `constructor` be <<constructor_of_externConstructorPrototypeIR, the constructor of  `externConstructorPrototypeIR` with type parameters  `typeParameterListIR`  and methods  `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
--
+
for each `externConstructorPrototypeIR` in `externConstructorPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_constructors_inst, $add_constructors_inst(IC~1~, cid^{asterisk}^, constructor^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList PARSER nameIR < typeParameterIR^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterListIR ) ( constructorParameterListIR ) { parserLocalDeclarationListIR parserStateListIR }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Check that `typeParameterIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group parserDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid_IR, $cid_IR(nameIR, constructorParameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `constructor` be `PARSER ( parameterListIR ) ( constructorParameterListIR ) { parserLocalDeclarationListIR parserStateListIR }`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_constructor_inst, $add_constructor_inst(IC~0~, cid, constructor)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList CONTROL nameIR < typeParameterIR^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterListIR ) ( constructorParameterListIR ) { controlLocalDeclarationListIR APPLY controlBodyIR }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Check that `typeParameterIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group controlDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid_IR, $cid_IR(nameIR, constructorParameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `constructor` be `CONTROL ( parameterListIR ) ( constructorParameterListIR ) { controlLocalDeclarationListIR APPLY controlBodyIR }`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_constructor_inst, $add_constructor_inst(IC~0~, cid, constructor)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `enumTypeDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`:
 .. If let `annotationList ENUM nameIR { nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeDeclarationIR`:
  ... Group enumTypeDeclarationIR-non-serializable:
   .... Let `nameIR~enum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~enum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `nameIR~enum_field~` be `nameIR ++ "." ++ nameIR~field~`.
--
+
for each `nameIR~field~` in `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `value~enum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~enum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `value~enum_field~` be `nameIR . nameIR~field~`.
--
+
for each `nameIR~field~` in `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_values_inst, $add_values_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR~enum_field~^{asterisk}^, value~enum_field~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR~enum~` be `ENUM nameIR { nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^ }`.
   .... Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~1~, nameIR, typeIR~enum~)>>`.
   .... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO'`, and ?().
 .. Else let `annotationList ENUM typeIR nameIR { nameIR~field~ = typedExpressionIR~field~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeDeclarationIR`:
  ... Group enumTypeDeclarationIR-serializable:
   .... Let <<Exprs_inst, `GLOBAL IC~0~ STO' |- typedExpressionIR~field~^{asterisk}^ ==> STO~1~ value~field~^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Let `nameIR~serenum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~serenum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `nameIR~serenum_field~` be `nameIR ++ "." ++ nameIR~field~`.
--
+
for each `nameIR~field~` in `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `value~serenum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~serenum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `value~serenum_field~` be `nameIR . nameIR~field~ # value~field~`.
--
+
for each `nameIR~field~` in `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^` and `value~field~` in `value~field~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_values_inst, $add_values_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR~serenum_field~^{asterisk}^, value~serenum_field~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR~serenum~` be `ENUM nameIR # typeIR { nameIR~field~ = value~field~ ;^{asterisk}^ }`.
   .... Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~1~, nameIR, typeIR~serenum~)>>`.
   .... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~1~`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList STRUCT nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > { typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group structTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `annotationList~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `annotationList~field~`, `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~field~`, and `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `annotationList~field~ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;` be `typeFieldIR`.
--
+
for each `typeFieldIR` in `typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeDefIR` be `STRUCT nameIR { typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;^{asterisk}^ } < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ >`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, typeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList HEADER nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > { typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group headerTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `annotationList~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `annotationList~field~`, `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~field~`, and `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `annotationList~field~ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;` be `typeFieldIR`.
--
+
for each `typeFieldIR` in `typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeDefIR` be `HEADER nameIR { typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;^{asterisk}^ } < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ >`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, typeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList HEADER_UNION nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > { typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group headerUnionTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `annotationList~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `annotationList~field~`, `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~field~`, and `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `annotationList~field~ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;` be `typeFieldIR`.
--
+
for each `typeFieldIR` in `typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeDefIR` be `HEADER_UNION nameIR { typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;^{asterisk}^ } < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ >`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, typeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `typedefDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`:
 .. If let `annotationList TYPEDEF typedefIR nameIR ;` be `typedefDeclarationIR`:
  ... Group typedefDeclarationIR-typedef:
   .... If let `typeIR` be `typedefIR`:
    ..... Let `typeIR~typedef~` be `TYPEDEF nameIR typeIR`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~typedef~)>>`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
   .... Else let `derivedTypeDeclarationIR` be `typedefIR`:
    ..... Let <<Decl_inst, `GLOBAL IC~0~ <<empty_store, $empty_store>> |- derivedTypeDeclarationIR ==> IC~local~ _ _^?^`>>.
    ..... Let `{ tid^{asterisk}^ }` be <<diff_set, the difference of the sets `<<dom_map, $dom_map<tid, typeDefIR>(IC~local~.GLOBAL.TYPE)>>` and `<<dom_map, $dom_map<tid, typeDefIR>(IC~0~.GLOBAL.TYPE)>>`>>.
    ..... Let!~type~ `[tid~newtype~]` be `tid^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let!~option~ `typeDefIR` be `<<find_typedef_inst, $find_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~local~, . tid~newtype~)>>`.
    ..... If let `typeIR` be `typeDefIR`:
     ...... Let `typeIR~typedef~` be `TYPEDEF nameIR typeIR`.
     ...... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~typedef~)>>`.
     ...... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
    ..... Else let `typeIR < tid'^{asterisk}^ , tid''^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeDefIR`:
     ...... Check that `tid'^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
     ...... Check that `tid''^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
     ...... Let `typeIR~typedef~` be `TYPEDEF nameIR typeIR < [ ] , [ ] > < [ ] >`.
     ...... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~typedef~)>>`.
     ...... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
 .. Else let `annotationList TYPE typeIR nameIR ;` be `typedefDeclarationIR`:
  ... Group typedefDeclarationIR-newtype:
   .... Let `typeIR~newtype~` be `TYPE nameIR typeIR`.
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~newtype~)>>`.
   .... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList PARSER nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group parserTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeIR~parser~` be `PARSER ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )`.
  ... Let `typeDefIR~parser~` be `typeIR~parser~ < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ >`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, typeDefIR~parser~)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList CONTROL nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group controlTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeIR~control~` be `CONTROL ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )`.
  ... Let `typeDefIR~control~` be `typeIR~control~ < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ >`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typedef_inst, $add_typedef_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, typeDefIR~control~)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and ?().
. Else if let `annotationList PACKAGE nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group packageTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, and `typeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR`, obtained by repeating:
