  ... Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_constructor_inst, $add_constructor_inst(IC~1~, cid, constructor~package~)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO'`, and ?().


relation Decls_inst: `p`, `IC'`, `STO'`, and `declarationIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `declarationIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `IC'`, `STO'`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `declarationIR~h~ :: declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `declarationIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons-none:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `p IC' STO' |- declarationIR~h~ ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR'^?^` is None.
  ... Let <<Decls_inst, `p IC~1~ STO~1~ |- declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~2~ STO~2~ declarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `declarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons-some:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `p IC' STO' |- declarationIR~h~ ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `?declarationIR~h_inst~` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Let <<Decls_inst, `p IC~1~ STO~1~ |- declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~2~ STO~2~ declarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `declarationIR~h_inst~ :: declarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Program_inst: `p4program`


. Group :
 .. Let `_` and `declarationIR^{asterisk}^ ;` be the result of <<Program_ok, typing the P4 program `p4program`>>.
 .. Let `IC~0~` be `<<empty_instantiationContext, $empty_instantiationContext>>`.
 .. Let `STO~0~` be `<<empty_store, $empty_store>>`.
 .. Let <<Decls_inst, `GLOBAL IC~0~ STO~0~ |- declarationIR^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^{asterisk}^`>>.
 .. Check that `declarationIR'^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Result in `IC~1~.GLOBAL.CONSTRUCTOR`, `IC~1~.GLOBAL.TYPE`, `IC~1~.GLOBAL.ROUTINE`, `IC~1~.GLOBAL.FRAME`, and `STO~1~`.


relation Bind_arg: `p~caller~`, `IC~caller~`, `p~callee~`, `IC~callee_0~`, `STO~0~`, `id`, and `argumentIR`


. Group :
 .. Let `IC~caller_inner~` be `<<enter_path, $enter_path(IC~caller~, id)>>`.
 .. Let <<Argument_inst, `p~caller~ IC~caller_inner~ STO~0~ |- argumentIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
 .. Let `IC~callee_1~` be `<<add_value_inst, $add_value_inst(p~callee~, IC~callee_0~, id, value)>>`.
 .. Result in `IC~callee_1~` and `STO~1~`.


relation Bind_args: `p~caller~`, `IC~caller~`, `p~callee~`, `IC~callee'~`, `STO'`, `id^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `id^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `IC~callee'~` and `STO'`.
. Else let `id~h~ :: id~t~^{asterisk}^` be `id^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Let!~type~ `argumentIR~h~ :: argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<Bind_arg, `p~caller~ IC~caller~ | p~callee~ IC~callee'~ STO' |- id~h~ argumentIR~h~ ==> IC~callee_1~ STO~1~`>>.
  ... Let <<Bind_args, `p~caller~ IC~caller~ | p~callee~ IC~callee_1~ STO~1~ |- id~t~^{asterisk}^ argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~callee_2~ STO~2~`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~callee_2~` and `STO~2~`.


relation Constructor_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, `constructor`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default'~^{asterisk}^`


. If let `EXTERN nameIR < typeParameterIR^{asterisk}^ > ( constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) { externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `constructor`:
 .. Group extern:
  ... Let `p~callee~` be `BLOCK`.
  ... Let `IC~callee_0~` be `<<inherit_instantiationContext, $inherit_instantiationContext(GLOBAL, IC)>>`.
  ... Let `IC~callee_1~` be `<<add_types_inst, $add_types_inst(p~callee~, IC~callee_0~, typeParameterIR^{asterisk}^, typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `(constructorParameterIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, constructorParameterIR~default~^{asterisk}^, value~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<align_cparams_with_args, $align_cparams_with_args(constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, and `id~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `id~aligned~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `_ _ _ id~aligned~ _` be `constructorParameterIR~aligned~`.
--
+
for each `constructorParameterIR~aligned~` in `constructorParameterIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let <<Bind_args, `p IC | p~callee~ IC~callee_1~ STO~0~ |- id~aligned~^{asterisk}^ argumentIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~callee_2~ STO~1~`>>.
  ... Let `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, and `id~cparam_default~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `id~cparam_default~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `_ _ _ id~cparam_default~ _` be `constructorParameterIR~default~`.
--
+
for each `constructorParameterIR~default~` in `constructorParameterIR~default~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `IC~callee_3~` be `<<add_values_inst, $add_values_inst(p~callee~, IC~callee_2~, id~cparam_default~^{asterisk}^, value~default~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let <<ExternMethods_inst, `IC~callee_3~ |- externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~callee_4~`>>.
  ... Let `object~extern~` be `EXTERN nameIR { IC~callee_4~.BLOCK.TYPE IC~callee_4~.BLOCK.FRAME IC~callee_4~.BLOCK.ROUTINE }`.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `object~extern~`.
. Else if let `PARSER ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ( constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) { parserLocalDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^ parserStateIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `constructor`:
 .. Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group parser:
  ... Let `p~callee~` be `BLOCK`.
  ... Let `IC~callee_0~` be `<<inherit_instantiationContext, $inherit_instantiationContext(GLOBAL, IC)>>`.
  ... Let `(constructorParameterIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, constructorParameterIR~default~^{asterisk}^, value~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<align_cparams_with_args, $align_cparams_with_args(constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, `_^{asterisk}^` be the list of `_`, and `id~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `id~aligned~`, obtained by repeating:
