  ... Let `IC~frame~` be `<<enter_inst, $enter_inst(IC~callee_0~)>>`.
  ... Let <<TableProperties_inst, `IC~frame~ STO~0~ |- tablePropertyListIR ==> STO~1~ tablePropertyListIR~inst~`>>.
  ... Let `tablePropertyListIR~dynamic~` be `<<init_table, $init_table(tablePropertyListIR~inst~)>>`.
  ... Let `frame'^{asterisk}^` be `IC~frame~.LOCAL.FRAMES`.
  ... Let!~type~ `frame :: _^{asterisk}^` be `frame'^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `object~table~` be `TABLE nameIR { frame tablePropertyListIR~dynamic~ }`.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `object~table~`.


relation SwitchCase_inst: `p`, `IC`, `store`, and `switchCaseIR`


. Group :
 .. If let `switchLabelIR : blockStatementIR` be `switchCaseIR`:
  ... Let `IC~switch~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `blockStatementIR`, under cursor `p`, instantiation context `IC`, and store `store`>>.
  ... Let!~type~ `blockStatementIR~inst~` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `switchLabelIR : blockStatementIR~inst~`.
 .. Else let `switchLabelIR :` be `switchCaseIR`:
  ... Result in `store` and `switchLabelIR :`.


relation SwitchCases_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `[ ]`.
. Else let `switchCaseIR~h~ :: switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<SwitchCase_inst, `p IC STO' |- switchCaseIR~h~ ==> STO~1~ switchCaseIR~h'~`>>.
  ... Let <<SwitchCases_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> STO~2~ switchCaseIR~t'~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~2~` and `switchCaseIR~h'~ :: switchCaseIR~t'~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Expr_eval: `p`, `EC`, `STO`, and `expressionIR # ( _ _ )`


. Let!~type~ `booleanLiteral` be `expressionIR`.
. Group literalExpressionIR-boolean:
 .. If `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `TRUE`:
  ... Result in the resulting store `STO` and expression result `B true`.
 .. Else `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `FALSE`:
  ... Result in the resulting store `STO` and expression result `B false`.


relation Stmt_eval: `p`, `EC`, `STO`, and `statementIR`


. Let!~type~ `conditionalStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
. Group conditionalStatementIR:
 .. If let `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~` be `conditionalStatementIR`:
  ... Let `STO~cond~` and `expressionResult` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR~cond~`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC`, and store `STO`>>.
  ... Else if `B true` is equal to `expressionResult`:
   .... Let `EC~then~`, `STO~then~`, and `statementResult` be the result of <<Stmt_eval, evaluating `statementIR~then~`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC`, and store `STO~cond~`>>.
   .... Result in 
* the resulting evaluation context `EC~then~`,
* store `STO~then~`,
* and statement result `statementResult`.
  ... Else if `B false` is equal to `expressionResult`:
   .... Result in 
* the resulting evaluation context `EC`,
* store `STO~cond~`,
* and statement result `CONT`.
  ... Else if `expressionResult` matches pattern `EXIT`:
   .... Result in 
* the resulting evaluation context `EC`,
* store `STO~cond~`,
* and statement result `EXIT`.
 .. Else let `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~ ELSE statementIR~else~` be `conditionalStatementIR`:
  ... Let `STO~cond~` and `expressionResult` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR~cond~`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC`, and store `STO`>>.
  ... Else if `B true` is equal to `expressionResult`:
   .... Let `EC~then~`, `STO~then~`, and `statementResult` be the result of <<Stmt_eval, evaluating `statementIR~then~`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC`, and store `STO~cond~`>>.
